            "raw_output": "130:class DataConfig:\n131-    \"\"\"What data to load, how to sample it in time, and how to reach it on S3.\n132-\n133-    Task-specific fields (label catalogs, alignment parameters, \u2026) do not belong here.\n134-    Subclass this in your app and pass the subclass to ``load_config(data_cls=...)``.\n135-    \"\"\"\n136-\n137-    # Fields holding a filesystem path. Relative values are resolved against the config\n138-    # file's own directory, so a checked-in config works from any working directory and\n139-    # on any machine \u2014 no absolute paths pointing into one user's home.\n140-    # A subclass that adds a path field must extend this, e.g.:\n141-    #     PATH_FIELDS = DataConfig.PATH_FIELDS + (\"my_catalog_path\",)\n142-    PATH_FIELDS: ClassVar[tuple[str, ...]] = (\n143-        \"train_data_path\",\n144-        \"valid_data_path\",\n145-        \"scalers_path\",\n146-        \"sdo_data_root_path\",\n147-    )\n148-\n149-    # --- Paths (relative paths are resolved against the config file's directory) ---\n150-    train_data_path: str\n151-    valid_data_path: str\n152-    scalers_path: str\n153-\n154-    # --- Input channels and temporal sampling ---\n155-    channels: List[str]\n156-    time_delta_input_minutes: List[int]\n157-    time_delta_target_minutes: int\n158-\n159-    # --- Local data ---\n160-    # Root prepended to relative local paths in the index. Ignored for s3:// paths.\n161-    sdo_data_root_path: Optional[str] = None\n162-\n163-    # --- S3 (used only when the index contains s3:// paths) ---\n164-    s3_anon: bool = False\n165-    # One of VALID_S3_MODES (above). \"download\" is recommended for NetCDF/HDF5.\n166-    s3_mode: str = \"download\"\n167-    # Required unless s3_mode is \"stream\". Budget ~1 GB per unique timestep.\n168-    # Left unset here, load_config() falls back to $SURYA_WS_CACHE_DIR.\n169-    s3_cache_dir: Optional[str] = None\n170-    s3_boto3_max_concurrency: int = 4   # parallel threads per multipart download\n---unknown key check---\n179:                f\"Unknown data.s3_mode {self.s3_mode!r}. \"\n226:                f\"Unknown training.deterministic {self.deterministic!r}. \"\n245:    Unknown keys are an error, not a silent no-op. A dropped key looks exactly like a\n253:    known = {f.name for f in dc_fields(cls)}\n265:        f.name for f in dc_fields(cls)",
