      "body": "Yes \u2014 `wave=1`, `no wave=0` is the standard convention here: the positive class (1) should be the thing you're trying to detect, and \"is there a wave\" is the natural framing for this task. It also lines up with `BCEWithLogitsLoss`/typical binary-classification metrics (precision/recall/AUC are usually reported with respect to class 1). That's what the plan already has:\n\n```python\nlabel_transform=lambda s: (s == \"wave\").astype(np.float32)\n```\n\nWant me to proceed with the edits (starting with `configs.py`)?",
      "time": 1789479214.3621192,
