            "raw_output": "1\timport numpy as np\n2\timport pandas as pd\n3\tfrom typing import Callable, Literal\n4\tfrom workshop_infrastructure.datasets.helio import HelioNetCDFDataset\n5\t\n6\t\n7\tclass waveDSDataset(HelioNetCDFDataset):\n8\t    \"\"\"\n9\t    Template child class of HelioNetCDFDataset showing how to build a downstream dataset.\n10\t    Extends the base class with a flare intensity label aligned to the Surya index.\n11\t\n12\t    All ``HelioNetCDFDataset`` keyword arguments (``index_path``, ``scalers``, ``channels``,\n13\t    ``s3_cache_dir``, etc.) are accepted via ``**kwargs`` and forwarded to the base class.\n14\t    ``load_forecast_frames`` defaults to ``False`` here (flare forecasting supplies its own\n15\t    labels, so future Surya frames are never fetched); pass it explicitly to override.\n16\t\n17\t    Additional Args:\n18\t        return_surya_stack: If True (default), include the Surya image stack in the returned dict.\n19\t            Set to False to return only the flare intensity label (useful for label inspection).\n20\t        max_number_of_samples: Cap the dataset length at this value. Useful for quick experiments.",
