      "body": "Now I have direct confirmation of the key mechanics: `helio.py:622-623` shows `time_delta_input_minutes[:-1]` are the historical candidates sampled, with the last entry always appended as \"now\" \u2014 so `time_delta_input_minutes=[-12, 0]` with `n_input_timestamps=2` deterministically yields `[t-12, t_now]` in that order (only one historical candidate to pick). And `builders.py:103` confirms `task_kwargs` override `_base_dataset_kwargs`, so I can pass `n_input_timestamps=2` straight into `build_helio_dataloaders()` without touching the shared `model.time_embedding.time_dim: 1` that the later full-Surya fine-tuning run depends on.\n\nI now have everything needed. Let me write the final plan."
