      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "The metrics in `metrics/template_metrics.py` are correct for this task \u2014 the loss is `binary_cross_entropy_with_logits` and the reported metrics are `BinaryAccuracy`/`BinaryAUROC`, both operating on raw logits (torchmetrics auto-sigmoids), matching what `BCEWithLogitsLoss` sees. That part's solid.\n\nI checked cell 23 in the notebook (the `make_metrics()` cell) \u2014 it's already using the classification version of `FlareMetrics` (BCE loss, accuracy, AUROC), not the old flare-regression one. So functionally nothing there needs to change for wave classification anymore.\n\nWhat I suspect you're actually flagging is naming, not function: the classes are still called `FlareMetrics`, `FlareLightningModule`, and `load_flare_config` \u2014 leftover names from the flare-forecasting template, even though their contents are now wave-classification logic. Let me check how far that naming leftover spreads before proposing a plan.",
      "id": "dba01324-5fc1-4e3c-bd2e-7ba0237476f3",
