      "body": "I found it. Three names are still branded \"Flare\" even though the content is now wave classification:\n\n- `configs.py`: `FlareDataConfig`, `load_flare_config` \u2014 docstring literally says \"flare-forecasting template app\"\n- `lightning_modules/pl_simple_baseline.py`: `FlareLightningModule` \u2014 docstring says \"flare prediction training\"\n- `metrics/template_metrics.py`: `FlareMetrics`\n\nNone of this is a correctness bug \u2014 the classes work fine for binary classification as they are, it's purely naming. There's also a batch key, `batch[\"forecast\"]`, used everywhere (`target = batch[\"forecast\"]`) that's semantically a leftover from \"forecasted flare intensity,\" now holding the wave/no-wave label.",
