      "body": "The deeper issue is that \"flare\" terminology runs through the whole fork \u2014 not just class names:\n\n- `wave_dataset.py`: docstrings (\"flare intensity label\", \"flare index\"), the error message `\"ds_flare_index_path must be provided for FlareDSDataset\"` (wrong class name too \u2014 copy-paste leftover), the internal column `normalized_intensity`, and the output key `sample[\"forecast\"]`\n- `pl_simple_baseline.py`: pulls the label via `batch[\"forecast\"]` in both `training_step` and `validation_step`\n- `configs.py`: `FlareDataConfig`, `load_flare_config`, field `flare_index_path`\n\nAll of this works correctly for wave classification today \u2014 it's naming, not a bug. But it is exactly what ADAPTING.md tells you to rename when forking (\"rename the classes that have 'Flare' or 'Template' in their names\").\n\nBefore I turn this into a plan, two things I don't want to assume:",
