      "body": "I'll ask directly in text since that tool isn't available here.\n\n**1. How far should the \"Flare\" \u2192 wave-classification renaming go?**\n- **Full cleanup** \u2014 rename everything: `FlareDataConfig`\u2192`WaveDataConfig`, `load_flare_config`\u2192`load_wave_config`, `FlareLightningModule`\u2192`WaveLightningModule`, `FlareMetrics`\u2192`WaveMetrics`, fix the stale docstrings/error strings in `wave_dataset.py`, and update the notebook accordingly.\n- **Class/function names only** \u2014 rename the four Python identifiers above, but leave the batch key (`\"forecast\"`) and internal column (`\"normalized_intensity\"`) alone, for a smaller diff.\n- **Leave naming as-is** \u2014 it's cosmetic, everything already works correctly for wave classification; skip it.\n\n**2. If we do rename the batch label key away from `\"forecast\"`, what should it become?**\n- `label`\n- `wave_label`\n- `target` (matches the local variable name already used inside `pl_simple_baseline.py`)\n- Keep `\"forecast\"` (pairs with either of the two more conservative options above)\n\nLet me know which combination you want, and whether `0_dataset_dataloader_template_diego.ipynb` (also touching this naming, per git status) and the still-broken `3_finetune_template_1D.py` (imports `downstream_apps.template.*`, unrelated stale bug flagged earlier) should be in scope too.",
