            "raw_output": "45:  # -- Downstream label alignment (flare catalog \u2192 Surya index) --\n46:  flare_index_path: ../data/lcpf_aia_waves.csv\n47:  ds_time_column: mid_time      # Column in the flare catalog used as the event timestamp\n49:  ds_match_direction: forward     # \"forward\": use solar state *before* the flare (causal)\n203:  s3_prefix: \"\"           # Key prefix (folder) within the bucket, e.g. flare/exp_001\n---configs.py---\n2:Task-specific configuration for the flare-forecasting template app.\n7:task: the flare catalog and how its events are aligned to the Surya index.\n32:class FlareDataConfig(DataConfig):\n33:    \"\"\"DataConfig plus the flare-catalog alignment settings used by ``FlareDSDataset``.\n39:    flare_index_path: str = \"\"\n44:    # \"forward\" uses the solar state *before* the flare (causal prediction).\n49:    # flare_index_path is a path, so it must join the base class's list to get the same\n51:    PATH_FIELDS: ClassVar[tuple[str, ...]] = DataConfig.PATH_FIELDS + (\"flare_index_path\",)\n55:# parsed into FlareDataConfig, so the four keys above are recognized instead of rejected.\n56:load_flare_config = partial(load_config, data_cls=FlareDataConfig)\n60:    \"FlareDataConfig\",\n61:    \"load_flare_config\",\n---0_dataset_dataloader_template_diego.ipynb---\n16:    \"This template uses a flare forecasting dataset as an example, casting the problem as an X-ray flux regression problem\"\n80:    \"# The config is the single source of truth. load_flare_config() parses it into a typed\\n\",\n87:    \"from downstream_apps.test.configs import load_flare_config\\n\",\n89:    \"cfg = load_flare_config(\\\"./configs/config_script.yaml\\\")\\n\",\n204:    \"    ds_flare_index_path=cfg.data.flare_index_path,\\n\",\n225:    \"Now we can test that the database is properly initialized and returns what is expected. In th case of the template, there are 6294 flares that take place during the training split\"\n477:    \"    ds_flare_index_path=cfg.data.flare_index_path,\\n\",\n763:    \"                        a diffuse, elongated wave arc from a compact flare.\\n\",\n810:    \"        # Filter condition: Must be large enough AND elongated (not a circular flare)\\n\",\n826:    \"    # Add a \\\"Flare\\\" (Compact, highly bright blob - should be rejected by aspect ratio)\\n\",\n---3_finetune_template_1D.py---\n45:from downstream_apps.template.configs import TrainingConfig, load_flare_config\n46:from downstream_apps.template.datasets.template_dataset import FlareDSDataset\n47:from downstream_apps.template.lightning_modules.pl_simple_baseline import FlareLightningModule\n48:from downstream_apps.template.metrics.template_metrics import FlareMetrics\n95:def _flare_label_transform(intensity: \"pd.Series\") -> \"pd.Series\":\n96:    \"\"\"Normalize flare peak intensity for the template task.\n113:    handled by build_helio_dataloaders(). Only the flare-specific arguments below are\n121:        FlareDSDataset,\n126:        label_transform=_flare_label_transform,\n127:        ds_flare_index_path=cfg.data.flare_index_path,\n141:        \"train_loss\": FlareMetrics(\"train_loss\"),\n143:        \"val_loss\": FlareMetrics(\"val_loss\"),\n144:        \"train_metrics\": FlareMetrics(\"train_metrics\"),\n145:        \"val_metrics\": FlareMetrics(\"val_metrics\"),\n151:            RegressionFlareModel,\n156:        model = RegressionFlareModel(n_input_timestamps * n_channels)\n158:        return FlareLightningModule(model, metrics, lr=cfg.learning_rate, batch_size=cfg.batch_size, preprocess_fn=preprocess_fn)\n182:    return FlareLightningModule(model, metrics, lr=cfg.learning_rate, batch_size=cfg.batch_size)\n255:    cfg = load_flare_config(args.config)",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01JyDB6oST7Tyo2FzHEck55F",
