umn `normalized_intensity` | `label` | `datasets/wave_dataset.py` (2 write sites, 1 read site) |\n| `FlareMetrics` | `WaveMetrics` | `metrics/template_metrics.py` |\n| `FlareLightningModule` | `WaveLightningModule` | `lightning_modules/pl_simple_baseline.py` |\n\nPlus prose fixes (docstrings, comments, one error message) wherever they say \"flare\nintensity\", \"flare catalog\", \"flare forecasting\", etc., reworded for wave classification.\nThe error message in `wave_dataset.py` also currently names the wrong class\n(`\"...for FlareDSDataset\"` when the class is `waveDSDataset`) \u2014 fixed as part of this pass.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. `test/configs.py`\n- `FlareDataConfig` \u2192 `WaveDataConfig`; `load_flare_config` \u2192 `load_wave_config`; field\n  `flare_index_path` \u2192 `wave_index_path` (update `PATH_FIELDS` tuple too); update module\n  docstring (\"flare-forecasting template app\" \u2192 wave-classification), `__all__`.\n\n### 2. `test/configs/config_script.yaml`\n- Key `flare_index_path` \u2192 `wave_index_path` under `data:`. Reword the two adjacent\n  comments (\"Downstream label alignment (flare catalog \u2192 Surya index)\", the\n  `ds_match_direction` comment) to drop \"flare\".\n\n### 3. `test/datasets/wave_dataset.py`\n- Constructor arg `ds_flare_index_path` \u2192 `ds_wave_index_path`.\n- Internal column `normalized_intensity` \u2192 `label` (the two assignment lines in `__init__`\n  and the read in `__getitem__`); `sample[\"forecast\"] = ...[\"label\"]` \u2014 the *output* key\n  name is unchanged, only the intermediate column.\n- Reword docstrings/comments (\"flare intensity label\" \u2192 \"wave/no-wave label\", \"flare index\"\n  \u2192 \"wave index\", \"flare forecasting supplies its own labels\" \u2192 task-neutral wording).\n- Fix the error message to name `waveDSDataset` (currently wrongly says `FlareDSDataset`).\n\n### 4. `test/metrics/template_metrics.py`\n- `FlareMetrics` \u2192 `WaveMetrics`. No logic changes \u2014 docstrings already describe BCE/\n  accuracy/AUROC correctly.\n\n### 5. `test/lightning_modules/pl_simple_baseline.py`\n- `FlareLightningModule` \u2192 `WaveLightningModule`. Reword module/class docstrings (\"flare\n  prediction training\" \u2192 \"wave classification training\"). Leave `batch[\"forecast\"]` reads\n  in `training_step`/`validation_step` untouched.\n\n### 6. `test/1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb`\n- Update the import cells and instantiations to the new names: `load_wave_config`,\n  `WaveMetrics`, `WaveLightningModule`, `ds_wave_index_path=cfg.data.wave_index_path`.\n- Update the `make_metrics()` cell's docstring and markdown cell 21's prose (\"FlareMetrics\n  has been converted...\" \u2192 \"WaveMetrics...\").\n\n### 7. `test/0_dataset_dataloader_template_diego.ipynb`\n- Same config-identifier updates as above (`load_wave_config`,\n  `ds_wave_index_path=cfg.data.wave_index_path`, both occurrences), since it shares the\n  same config module and would otherwise break after the rename. Reword the intro markdown\n  line describing the dataset as a \"flare forecasting dataset\" example.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `grep -rniE \"flare\" downstream_apps/test --include=\"*.py\" --include=\"*.yaml\"` on the\n  edited files should only still show `models/simple_baseline.py` (kept intentionally) and\n  `3_finetune_template_1D.py` (unrelated pre-existing bug, out of scope).\n- In the `jovyan-Surya_WS` kernel, run `0_dataset_dataloader_template_diego.ipynb` cells\n  one-by-one through the dataset-build cells \u2014 confirms `load_wave_config` /\n  `ds_wave_index_path` work end-to-end.\n- Run `1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb` cells one-by-one from the top through the\n  `trainer.fit(...)` cell \u2014 confirms the renamed `WaveMetrics`/`WaveLightningModule`\n  imports resolve and training still completes without error.\n"
