92 task-neutral wording).\n63\t- Fix the error message to name `waveDSDataset` (currently wrongly says `FlareDSDataset`).\n64\t\n65\t### 4. `test/metrics/template_metrics.py`\n66\t- `FlareMetrics` \u2192 `WaveMetrics`. No logic changes \u2014 docstrings already describe BCE/\n67\t  accuracy/AUROC correctly.\n68\t\n69\t### 5. `test/lightning_modules/pl_simple_baseline.py`\n70\t- `FlareLightningModule` \u2192 `WaveLightningModule`. Reword module/class docstrings (\"flare\n71\t  prediction training\" \u2192 \"wave classification training\"). Leave `batch[\"forecast\"]` reads\n72\t  in `training_step`/`validation_step` untouched.\n73\t\n74\t### 6. `test/1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb`\n75\t- Update the import cells and instantiations to the new names: `load_wave_config`,\n76\t  `WaveMetrics`, `WaveLightningModule`, `ds_wave_index_path=cfg.data.wave_index_path`.\n77\t- Update the `make_metrics()` cell's docstring and markdown cell 21's prose (\"FlareMetrics\n78\t  has been converted...\" \u2192 \"WaveMetrics...\").\n79\t\n80\t### 7. `test/0_dataset_dataloader_template_diego.ipynb`\n81\t- Same config-identifier updates as above (`load_wave_config`,\n82\t  `ds_wave_index_path=cfg.data.wave_index_path`, both occurrences), since it shares the\n83\t  same config module and would otherwise break after the rename. Reword the intro markdown\n84\t  line describing the dataset as a \"flare forecasting dataset\" example.\n85\t\n86\t## Verification\n87\t\n88\t- `grep -rniE \"flare\" downstream_apps/test --include=\"*.py\" --include=\"*.yaml\"` on the\n89\t  edited files should only still show `models/simple_baseline.py` (kept intentionally) and\n90\t  `3_finetune_template_1D.py` (unrelated pre-existing bug, out of scope).\n91\t- In the `jovyan-Surya_WS` kernel, run `0_dataset_dataloader_template_diego.ipynb` cells\n92\t  one-by-one through the dataset-build cells \u2014 confirms `load_wave_config` /\n93\t  `ds_wave_index_path` work end-to-end.\n94\t- Run `1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb` cells one-by-one from the top through the\n95\t  `trainer.fit(...)` cell \u2014 confirms the renamed `WaveMetrics`/`WaveLightningModule`\n96\t  imports resolve and training still completes without error.\n97\t",
