      "time": 1789575367.9439301,
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "Good, I checked your repo state and it matches what you described exactly:\n\n- Remote `origin` \u2192 your fork (`dlloveras/surya_workshop2026.git`).\n- Local `main` is tracking `origin/main` but is **behind by 16 commits** \u2014 that's the sync you did on GitHub, not yet pulled locally.\n- You're currently on `downstream/wave_classification`, which is up to date with its remote.\n- One stash exists: `stash@{0}: WIP on wave_classification: 49f5eb7...` \u2014 made from this same branch, so popping it back here is the simple case (no cross-branch stash weirdness).\n- Note: the untracked files (`1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb`, etc.) are **not** part of the stash (a plain `git stash` doesn't grab untracked files unless you pass `-u`), so they'll just sit there unaffected through all of this \u2014 nothing to worry about with those.\n\nHere's the sequence:\n\n**1. Update your local `main` from your GitHub fork:**\n```bash\ngit checkout main\ngit pull origin main\n```\nThis moves local `main` forward to match `origin/main`. Since local `main` has no commits of its own (only \"behind\", not \"ahead\"), this will be a clean fast-forward \u2014 no merge conflicts possible here.\n\n**2. Go back to your working branch and bring `main`'s new commits into it:**\n```bash\ngit checkout downstream/wave_classification\ngit merge main\n```\nThis merges the 16 new commits into your branch. Your working tree is currently clean (everything's stashed), so this merge can't conflict with uncommitted work \u2014 it can only conflict if the *committed* history diverged, which `git status` doesn't suggest here.\n\n**3. Restore your stashed work on top:**\n```bash\ngit stash pop\n```\nThis reapplies your stashed changes to the now-updated branch, and removes the stash entry if it applies cleanly.\n\n**If step 3 reports conflicts:** it'll tell you which files. Resolve them by hand (`git status` shows conflict markers to fix), then `git add <file>` on each resolved file. In that case the stash is **not** auto-dropped \u2014 run `git stash drop` afterward once you've confirmed the resolution looks right.\n\nWant me to run step 1 now, or would you rather run these yourself and have me check the result after each step?",
