    {
      "id": "36dadf94-306b-4454-a6e4-9c4df72902f7",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false,
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "All confirmed against the actual source. Here's the walkthrough, ordered by the notebook's execution path, with every LoRA/HelioSpectformer-adjacent piece checked against what's actually on disk.\n\n## The notebook's job\n\n`2_finetune_template_1D_diego.ipynb` builds the real Surya pipeline: load config \u2192 build wave dataset/dataloaders \u2192 construct `HelioSpectformer1D` (366M-param backbone + classification head) \u2192 load pretrained weights \u2192 apply LoRA/freeze regime \u2192 wire up `WaveMetrics` + `WaveLightningModule` \u2192 train with `Trainer(precision=\"bf16-mixed\")`. It's copy-pasted from the flare template (`downstream_apps/template/`), and several import lines still point at the flare app or use flare-era names that don't exist. I traced each one against the actual files. **Six confirmed bugs**, all will raise before training starts:\n\n**1. Cell `63c1fe60` \u2014 wrong config loader (app-level).**\n```python\nfrom downstream_apps.template.configs import load_flare_config\ncfg = load_flare_config(\"./configs/config_script.yaml\")\n```\n`load_flare_config` parses `data:` into `FlareDataConfig` (fields: `flare_index_path`, ...). Your YAML's `data:` section has `wave_index_path`/`ds_class_column` (defined in `downstream_apps/test/configs.py`'s `WaveDataConfig`). `load_config`'s `_from_dict` rejects unknown keys outright \u2014 this will raise `\"Unrecognized key(s) in 'data:' section... wave_index_path, ds_class_column\"` immediately.\n**Fix:** `from downstream_apps.test.configs import load_wave_config` / `cfg = load_wave_config(...)`.\n\n**2. Cell `34db2cc6` \u2014 dataset class doesn't exist at that path.**\n```python\nfrom downstream_apps.template.datasets.template_dataset import waveDSDataset\n```\nThat module defines `FlareDSDataset`, not `waveDSDataset` \u2014 `ImportError`. The real class is `downstream_apps/test/datasets/wave_dataset.py:waveDSDataset` (lowercase `w`, confirmed \u2014 that one's actually named that way).\n**Fix:** `from downstream_apps.test.datasets.wave_dataset import waveDSDataset`.\n\n**3. Cell `70e9c5b2` \u2014 dataloader kwargs use flare-era names and drop the required label wiring.**\n```python\nds_flare_index_path=cfg.data.flare_index_path,   # wrong name + attribute doesn't exist on WaveDataConfig\n```\n`waveDSDataset.__init__` (the real one) takes `ds_wave_index_path`, `ds_time_column`, `ds_class_column`, `ds_time_tolerance`, `ds_match_direction` \u2014 and **raises `ValueError` if `ds_class_column` is missing**. This cell passes neither `ds_wave_index_path` nor `ds_class_column`; `ds_flare_index_path` just falls through `**kwargs` into `HelioNetCDFDataset.__init__`, which doesn't expect it \u2192 `TypeError`.\n**Fix:**\n```python\nds_wave_index_path=cfg.data.wave_index_path,\nds_time_column=cfg.data.ds_time_column,\nds_class_column=cfg.data.ds_class_column,\nds_time_tolerance=cfg.data.ds_time_tolerance,\nds_match_direction=cfg.data.ds_match_direction,\n```\nYou'll also want a `label_transform` if `ds_class_column`'s raw values aren't already 0/1 floats \u2014 check what `class` actually contains in `../data/lcpf_aia_waves.csv` (the YAML comment says \"wave or on wave\"; if it's a string, add e.g. `label_transform=lambda s: (s == \"wave\").astype(np.float32)` as in notebook 1).\n\n**4. Cell `34c502ec` \u2014 metrics class, wrong app + wrong casing.**\n```python\nfrom downstream_apps.template.metrics.template_metrics import waveMetrics\n```\nThat module defines `FlareMetrics`. The real, already-adapted classification metrics live at `downstream_apps/test/metrics/template_metrics.py:WaveMetrics` (capital W) \u2014 I read it in full: it's correctly built for this task (BCE-with-logits for `train_loss`/`val_loss`, `BinaryAccuracy`+`BinaryAUROC` for `train_metrics`/`val_metrics`).\n**Fix:** `from downstream_apps.test.metrics.template_metrics import WaveMetrics`.\n\n**5. Cell `9d730cf3` \u2014 right module, wrong class name casing.**\n```python\nfrom downstream_apps.test.lightning_modules.pl_simple_baseline import waveLightningModule\n```\nThe module path is correct, but the class is `WaveLightningModule` (capital W) \u2014 I confirmed this by reading the file. `ImportError`.\n**Fix:** `from downstream_apps.test.lightning_modules.pl_simple_baseline import WaveLightningModule`.\n\n**6. Cell `b008c604` \u2014 same hardcoded-epochs bug you already fixed in notebook 1.**\n```python\nmax_epochs = 4\n```\nShould be `max_epochs = cfg.max_epochs` for the same reason as before.\n\n## The one bug outside the notebook: LoRA target_modules in the YAML\n\nThis is the part you specifically asked about. `configs/config_script.yaml`:\n```yaml\ntarget_modules: [q_proj, v_proj, k_proj, out_proj, fc1, fc2]\n```\nSurya's vendored backbone **fuses q/k/v into one `nn.Linear` named `attn.qkv`**, with output projection at `attn.proj` \u2014 there is no `q_proj`/`k_proj`/`v_proj`/`out_proj` anywhere in this model (confirmed against `LoraAdapterConfig`'s own default in `workshop_infrastructure/configs.py`, which is `[\"fc1\", \"fc2\", \"attn.qkv\", \"attn.proj\"]`, and against CLAUDE.md). `apply_peft_lora()` / PEFT only errors when **none** of `target_modules` match anything \u2014 since `fc1`/`fc2` do match, those four wrong names are **silently ignored**. Net effect: LoRA adapters are only being fit on the MLP layers, never on attention \u2014 a real, silent under-adaptation, not a crash.\n**Fix:**\n```yaml\ntarget_modules: [fc1, fc2, attn.qkv, attn.proj]\n```\n\n## What's already correct (verified, not just inferred)\n\n- `ecbb6638`'s LoRA/head markdown and cell `677a4319`'s freeze/LoRA branching logic are generic and correct as written \u2014 no wave-specific changes needed.\n- `HelioSpectformer1D`'s `head_unembed = nn.Linear(embed_dim, 1)` + `.squeeze(dim=1)` (in `finetune_models.py`) gives exactly the `(B,)`/`(B,1)`-logit shape `WaveMetrics` and `WaveLightningModule` expect (target is `.unsqueeze(1)`'d, loss is `BCEWithLogitsLoss`). `num_outputs=1` in cell `d1941589` is correct for this task, unchanged from the flare template \u2014 a single logit is right for binary classification too.\n- `dtype=cfg.dtype` passed as a plain string into `HelioSpectformer1D.from_config` looks like a type mismatch (`HelioSpectFormer.__init__` types it as `torch.dtype`) but its docstring says the param is accepted only for cross-file signature compatibility and unused internally \u2014 inert either way, matches the template exactly, not a bug.\n- `discover_head_modules()`/PEFT's `modules_to_save` mechanics, and the three regimes (`use_lora`/`freeze_backbone`), require no changes for a classification head \u2014 the `head_` convention doesn't care what loss sits on top.\n\n## Net picture\n\nThe notebook is a nearly line-for-line flare\u2192wave port, and the copy-paste missed exactly the lines that name the flare app/classes explicitly (config loader, dataset, metrics, Lightning module) plus one leftover kwarg block. None of these are subtle \u2014 each one raises immediately (`ImportError`/`ValueError`/config-validation error) the first time you run past it, so you'll hit them in order, top to bottom, as soon as you execute. The LoRA `target_modules` bug is the only one that fails silently rather than loudly \u2014 worth fixing before you trust any trained result from this notebook, since right now attention layers get zero adaptation.\n\nWant me to apply these six notebook fixes plus the YAML `target_modules` fix now?",
      "type": "msg",
      "time": 1789584930.6714225
    },
