      "body": "`numpy` isn't imported anywhere in this notebook yet, so add it in the imports cell too. Two edits:\n\n**Cell `4ed04321`** (imports) \u2014 add `import numpy as np`:\n```python\nimport torch\nimport numpy as np\nimport yaml\n```\n\n**Cell `70e9c5b2`** \u2014 add `label_transform` as one of the \"Downstream (DS) specific parameters\", alongside the other `ds_*` kwargs (order doesn't matter, but grouping it there matches notebook 1's convention):\n```python\ntrain_data_loader, val_data_loader = build_helio_dataloaders(\n    cfg,\n    waveDSDataset,\n    scalers=scalers,\n    num_workers=4,          # fewer workers than the script: notebooks start faster\n    #### Downstream (DS) specific parameters\n    return_surya_stack=True,\n    max_number_of_samples=10,\n    ds_wave_index_path=cfg.data.wave_index_path,\n    ds_time_column=cfg.data.ds_time_column,\n    ds_class_column=cfg.data.ds_class_column,\n    ds_time_tolerance=cfg.data.ds_time_tolerance,\n    ds_match_direction=cfg.data.ds_match_direction,\n    label_transform=lambda s: (s == \"wave\").astype(np.float32),\n)\n```\n\nIt's a `waveDSDataset.__init__` keyword, applied to the `ds_class_column` series at dataset-construction time (`self.ds_index[\"label\"] = label_transform(self.ds_index[ds_class_column])` in `wave_dataset.py`) \u2014 so it belongs in this same call, not somewhere later in the notebook."
