    {
      "body": "All three agents in, plus my own measurements. The decisive numbers:\n\n- **Throughput: 3.1 s/sample** (3.05 s/step at B=1, 6.23 s at B=2 \u2014 linear, compute-bound)\n- **VRAM: B=2 \u2192 42.4 GB reserved of 47.7 (89%); B=4 \u2192 OOM.** So B=2 is the max, and effective batch must come from gradient accumulation.\n- **LoRA with correct targets = 3,157,761 trainable**, exactly matching CLAUDE.md \u2014 vs the 2.7 M your diverged run logged.\n- **Dataset: 1,232 train / 27 val** matched samples, 50/50 balanced \u2014 but negatives are the *same event's pre-onset frame*, 1 h earlier.\n\nOne unknown still governs the schedule: how many needed frames are already in the 2 TB cache.",
