              "questions": "[{\"question\":\"Validation is only 27 samples (13 wave / 14 no-wave), so one sample = 3.7% of accuracy and val_loss-based checkpointing is nearly a coin flip between epochs. How should I handle it?\",\"header\":\"Validation set\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Val + test report\",\"description\":\"Use the official 27-sample val for monitoring/checkpointing, and additionally evaluate the best checkpoint on the official 54-sample test split for a final, less-noisy number. Held-out total 81. Costs ~60 GB extra download, no extra training time. Keeps the official day-disjoint splits intact.\"},{\"label\":\"Official val only\",\"description\":\"Use only the official 27-sample val split. Most conservative and standard, nothing extra to download, but val curves will be visibly noisy and epoch-to-epoch checkpoint selection is weak.\"},{\"label\":\"Re-split for bigger val\",\"description\":\"Re-partition from surya_aws_s3_full_index.csv to build a larger validation set, recovering the 254 catalog rows in 2012/2022 that are absent from all official splits. Gives a few hundred val samples, but breaks comparability with the official split and costs extra setup time.\"}]},{\"question\":\"The label-to-image match tolerance is currently 4 days. In practice 99.2% of matches land within 15 min, but the 10 loosest train matches (up to 1 day off) are 9-to-1 'no wave', which is what skews the balance to 612/619 instead of an exact 611/611.\",\"header\":\"Match tolerance\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Tighten to 15min\",\"description\":\"Set ds_time_tolerance to 15min. Costs 10 train samples and 2 val samples, restores exact 611/611 class balance, and guarantees every label is paired with an image within one Surya cadence step of the catalog timestamp. More defensible pairing.\"},{\"label\":\"Keep 4d\",\"description\":\"Leave ds_time_tolerance at 4d as currently configured. Keeps 1231 train samples, but a handful of labels are matched to images up to a day away, and those stragglers bias the class balance slightly toward 'no wave'.\"}]},{\"question\":\"The corrected settings (time_dim 2 for the 26-channel tokenizer, fixed LoRA target_modules, larger max_samples, safe learning rate) have to live somewhere. configs/config_script.yaml is currently shared by your notebooks.\",\"header\":\"Config strategy\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Fix shared + new scale cfg\",\"description\":\"Fix the outright bugs (time_dim/time_delta alignment, LoRA target_modules) in place in config_script.yaml with the old values kept as comments, so your notebooks become correct too; add a separate new config for the full-scale run settings (max_samples, lr, epochs). Notebooks and scripts stay consistent.\"},{\"label\":\"New config only\",\"description\":\"Leave config_script.yaml completely untouched and put everything corrected into a brand-new config file used only by the new scripts. Zero risk to existing notebooks, but 2_finetune_template_1D_diego.ipynb keeps loading a config that silently randomizes the tokenizer unless you also repoint it.\"}]},{\"question\":\"If the 18 hours run short, what should I protect at the expense of the rest?\",\"header\":\"Time priority\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Full-set run first\",\"description\":\"Prioritize one good Surya run on all ~1231 training samples (about 64 min/epoch), so the headline result is a real fine-tune on the full dataset. The data-scaling curve gets whatever time is left and may be incomplete.\"},{\"label\":\"Scaling curve first\",\"description\":\"Prioritize the data-scaling study (e.g. 128 / 384 / full images) so you can answer whether val loss improves with more data, even if the largest run gets fewer epochs and no single run is trained to convergence.\"},{\"label\":\"Baselines + diagnosis\",\"description\":\"Prioritize finishing tasks 1.1 and 1.2 and a fully-characterized baseline (learning curves, overfitting analysis) before spending anything substantial on Surya. Safest for having complete, explainable results, weakest on the foundation-model headline.\"}]}]"
            }
