        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "raw_input": {
              "replace_all": false,
              "new_string": "**RAM is the real danger.** `ts` is `(B,13,2,4096,4096)` float32 = **1.74 GB per sample**.\nWorst-case RSS \u2248 `num_workers \u00d7 prefetch_factor \u00d7 batch_size \u00d7 1.74 GB`. At the config's\n`num_workers: 8` with default `prefetch_factor=2` and batch 2 that is **56 GB**, before the\nmain process, pinned-memory copies and page cache. This is the \"collapse the AWS machine\"\nrisk, and it must be bounded explicitly rather than left to defaults.\n\n**The pipeline is CPU/IO-balanced against the GPU, not GPU-dominated** \u2014 measured per sample:\n2 \u00d7 4.7 s to read 13 channels from a cached NetCDF (EFS+HDF5 gives ~185 MB/s per stream, well\nbelow `dd`'s 585 MB/s) + 4.7 s signum-log + 0.4 s z-score = **15.2 s of CPU per sample**. To feed\none sample per 3.1 s therefore needs **\u2265 5 workers**, and aggregate EFS demand at 8 workers\n(~1.5 GB/s) may itself throttle. Consequence: **`num_workers=8, prefetch_factor=1` is the right\noperating point** \u2014 more CPU parallelism *and less* memory than `6 \u00d7 2` (27.8 GB vs 41.8 GB) \u2014 and\nepoch time should be budgeted at the data-limited rate (~3.6 s/sample, **~75-80 min for the full\n1231**), not the ideal 3.1. Set `OMP_NUM_THREADS=2` so 8 workers do not oversubscribe 16 CPUs.",
              "file_path": "/home/jovyan/.claude/plans/i-m-running-a-ipynb-melodic-seal.md",
              "old_string": "**RAM is the real danger.** `ts` is `(B,13,2,4096,4096)` float32 = **1.74 GB per sample**.\nWorst-case RSS \u2248 `num_workers \u00d7 prefetch_factor \u00d7 batch_size \u00d7 1.74 GB`. At the config's\n`num_workers: 8` with default `prefetch_factor=2` and batch 2 that is **56 GB**, before the\nmain process, pinned-memory copies and page cache. This is the \"collapse the AWS machine\"\nrisk, and it must be bounded explicitly rather than left to defaults."
            },
