    {
      "type": "msg",
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1789654794.4157665,
      "body": "A couple of comments to you to take in mind.\n-regarding your comment \"the same event's pre-onset frame, 1 hour earlier, same active region\" actually I want the running difference to be consecutive images in the bucket. I've been told that they are separed by around 12 minutes, NOT 1 hours. that is key because the waves are visible during aorund 40 minutes, please check.\n-You don't need to download all images requiered for the entire dataset, you can decrease the size if necesarry. We are still exploring. This is not going to be final.\n-You can modify the lora rank if necessary. that may alow you to increase batch size.\n-check if the surya head is ok for classification.\n-check if we need a lower amount of training variables for task 1.1\nI'm ok with your other comments.",
