      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "body": "Yes, active \u2014 I was interrupted mid-turn, so nothing had run yet. Let me verify your points now.\n\nFirst, an important distinction I should have made clearer, because I think we're talking about two different 12-vs-60-minute things and only one of them is a disagreement:\n\n- **The running difference input** is already `[-12, 0]` \u2014 two *consecutive bucket frames, 12 min apart*. That's exactly what you want, and it's what's in the plan.\n- **The 1 hour** was about something else: which *timestamps get labeled*. The catalog puts `wave` at `start_time + 30 min` and `no wave` at `start_time \u2212 30 min`, so the positive and negative *samples* of one event sit 1 h apart from each other. That's a property of the label file, not of the running difference.\n\nLet me confirm both, and check the wave-visibility window against that +30 min sampling point.",
      "type": "msg",
      "time": 1789656060.029506,
      "id": "d581428d-fa52-49ac-8245-8f721d32dc8e",
