      "body": "Plan updated. The main structural changes from your feedback:\n\n**Dataset shrunk to 384 train / 27 val / 54 test** (seeded, event-level stratified). That's 460 GB instead of 1.35 TB \u2014 13 min of download \u2014 and it buys *far* more epochs per run: 14-30 epochs each instead of 3-4 on the full set, which gives convergent curves rather than truncated ones.\n\n**Task 1 now reads AIA193 only**, making the whole baseline arm ~12.7\u00d7 cheaper and freeing time for the visibility scan.\n\n**`penultimate_linear_layer: false` becomes the default**, cutting trainable params 3,157,761 \u2192 1,518,081 with no loss of capacity \u2014 and it's A/B'd so the claim gets tested rather than assumed. LoRA rank r \u2208 {4, 8} moves into the ablation slot as a capacity knob.\n\n**The wave-visibility scan is promoted ahead of all GPU work.** If RD contrast peaks near onset +12 min and has decayed by +30, then label *timing* \u2014 not sample count \u2014 is why the baseline can't generalize, and the fix is a new catalog CSV with a better positive offset. Two CPU-hours to test something that would otherwise silently cap every result in the remaining 16.\n\nTwo open items are listed at the end of the plan with defaults (validation strategy, match tolerance) \u2014 tell me if you want them different, otherwise I'll use the defaults.",
