              "command": "python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"4_finetune_wave_1D.py\")\ns = p.read_text()\n\n# build_trainer must hand back the CSV logger: Trainer.log_dir returns the FIRST logger's\n# directory, which is wandb's when wandb is enabled, not where metrics.csv lives.\nold = '''    loggers.append(CSVLogger(\"runs\", name=run_name))\n'''\nnew = '''    csv_logger = CSVLogger(\"runs\", name=run_name)\n    loggers.append(csv_logger)\n'''\nassert s.count(old) == 1\ns = s.replace(old, new)\n\nold = ''') -> Tuple[L.Trainer, ModelCheckpoint, ResourceGuard]:\n    \"\"\"Configure loggers, callbacks and the Trainer.\"\"\"'''\nnew = ''') -> Tuple[L.Trainer, ModelCheckpoint, ResourceGuard, CSVLogger]:\n    \"\"\"Configure loggers, callbacks and the Trainer.\n\n    The CSVLogger is returned explicitly rather than being fished back out of the Trainer:\n    ``Trainer.log_dir`` is the *first* logger's directory, which is wandb's whenever wandb is\n    enabled, so reading ``metrics.csv`` from it would silently find nothing and the\n    training-curve figure would come out empty.\n    \"\"\"'''\nassert s.count(old) == 1\ns = s.replace(old, new)\n\nold = \"    return trainer, checkpoint_cb, guard\\n\"\nnew = \"    return trainer, checkpoint_cb, guard, csv_logger\\n\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\ns = s.replace(old, new)\n\nold = \"    trainer, checkpoint_cb, guard = build_trainer(cfg, args, run_name)\"\nnew = \"    trainer, checkpoint_cb, guard, csv_logger = build_trainer(cfg, args, run_name)\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\ns = s.replace(old, new)\n\nold = \"        figures = plot_run(run_name, Path(trainer.log_dir or \\\".\\\"), evals, RESULTS_DIR)\"\nnew = \"        figures = plot_run(run_name, Path(csv_logger.log_dir), evals, RESULTS_DIR)\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\ns = s.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"log_dir bug fixed\")\nPY\n/home/jovyan/envs/surya_WS/bin/python -m py_compile 4_finetune_wave_1D.py && echo \"compiles ok\"; tail -1 /home/jovya