      "metadata": {
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "raw_output": "Exit code 1\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 52, in <module>\nKeyError: 'achieved_offsets_median'",
            "title": "python - <<'PY' from pathlib import Path import json R = Path(\"experiments/results\") bs = json.loads((R / \"baseline_study.json\").read_text()) vis = json.loads((R / \"wave_visibility.json\").read_text()) rep = bs[\"reproduction\"] curve = bs[\"learning_curve\"] lines = [\"\", \"## Results so far (tasks 1.1 and 1.2; task 2.4 is in `results/task_2_4_answer.md`)\", \"\"] lines += [ \"### 1.1 \u2014 the wave is visible in the representation the baseline is given\", \"\", \"`results/task_1_1_wave_visibility.png` shows three matched wave / no-wave pairs at three\", \"levels of detail: AIA193 at *t*, the full-resolution running difference, and the\", \"32x-mean-pooled 128x128 map that `RunningDifferenceLogisticModel` actually consumes.\", \"Because the negative is the same event one hour earlier, the comparison is controlled for\", \"active region, limb position and epoch of the solar cycle.\", \"\", \"Max |pooled| in the wave sample against its own matched control:\", \"\", \"| event | wave | no wave | ratio |\", \"|---|---|---|---|\", \"| 2010-06-12T00:30 | 1.5719 | 0.3588 | 4.4x |\", \"| 2010-08-07T17:55 | 1.1573 | 0.1422 | 8.1x |\", \"| 2010-12-31T04:18 | 0.4204 | 0.1814 | 2.3x |\", \"\", \"So the signal survives the 32x pooling. Whatever limits the baseline, it is not that the\", \"wave is invisible at 128x128.\", \"\", \"**Caveat worth carrying into any conclusion.** The bright running-difference structure is\", \"dominated by the eruption *source region* \u2014 a compact brightening plus a dimming \u2014 not by\", \"the propagating wave front. A classifier trained on this may be learning \\\"is there a\", \"bright compact eruption right now\\\", which is correlated with but not the same as \\\"is there\", \"an EUV wave\\\".\", \"\", ] best = vis[\"best_offset_min\"] at30 = vis[\"median_pooled_snr_at_catalog_offset_30\"] lines += [ \"### 1.1 extended \u2014 is +30 min a good place to sample a positive?\", \"\", \"This was the plan's largest scientific risk: positives sit at onset +30 min, so their\", \"running difference spans +18 to +30 min, and if EUV wave contrast peaked early and decayed\", \"by then, the *label timing* rather than the sample count would be the binding constraint.\", \"\", f\"Measured on {vis['n_events']} events, contrast against each event's own quiet-Sun control\", \"(its negative sample's running difference at -30 min), on-disk only:\", \"\", \"| requested offset | achieved | median pooled SNR |\", \"|---|---|---|\", ] for off, snr in vis[\"median_pooled_snr_by_offset\"].items(): lines.append(f\"| +{off} min | +{vis['achieved_offsets_median'][str(off)]:.0f} min | {snr:.2f} |\") lines += [ \"\", f\"**The risk did not materialize, and the effect runs the other way.** Contrast *rises* with\", f\"offset: it is 1.49 at +12 min and peaks at {vis['best_median_pooled_snr']:.2f} at \" f\"+{best:.0f} min. At the catalog's +30 min it is {at30:.2f} \u2014 \" f\"{vis['decay_from_best_to_30_pct']:.0f}% below the peak, still 2.5x the quiet Sun.\", \"So +30 min is an acceptable sampling point, the re-timed catalog the plan held in reserve\", \"is unnecessary, and sample count remains the binding constraint.\", \"\", ] lines += [ \"### 1.2 \u2014 the 10-sample run was memorization, and more images do help\", \"\", \"**The overfit reproduces.** Refitting on the 10 samples `max_samples: 10` actually selects\", f\"(the earliest 5 event pairs, {rep['dates'][0]} to {rep['dates'][-1]} \u2014 `waveDSDataset`\", \"head-slices a time-sorted frame, so the cap is a chronological bias, not a sample):\", \"\", f\"- training loss {rep['train_loss_first']:.3f} -> {rep['train_loss_last']:.4f}, \" f\"training accuracy {rep['train_accuracy_last']:.2f}\", f\"- validation loss {rep['val_loss_first']:.3f} -> {rep['val_loss_last']:.3f} (rising)\", f\"- validation AUROC below chance throughout, and **exactly frozen over the last two thirds\", f\" of training** (spread {rep['val_auroc_tail_spread']:.4f})\", \"\", \"The frozen AUROC is the diagnostic part: the *ranking* of the validation samples stops\", \"changing, so the model is only rescaling a direction fixed in the first few steps. It does\", \"not freeze from epoch 0 as `version_3`'s did, because validation here is the 24-sample\", \"balanced split rather than `version_3`'s 27-sample set at the looser 4-day tolerance \u2014 so\", \"the fingerprint differs while the diagnosis stands.\", \"\", \"**And validation loss does improve with more images.** Event-level stratified, nested\", \"subsets, median over 5 seeds:\", \"\", \"| N | best val BCE | val AUROC |\", \"|---|---|---|\", ] for c in curve: lines.append(f\"| {c['n_train']} | {c['best_val_loss_median']:.4f} | \" f\"{c['best_val_auroc_median']:.3f} |\") lines += [ \"\", f\"`ConstantProbabilityModel`, which learns only the base rate, scores \" f\"{bs['constant_probability']['val_loss']:.4f} \u2014 the same as chance (ln 2 = 0.6931) on a\", \"balanced split. The running-difference baseline reaches **0.5607 BCE / 0.812 AUROC** at\", \"N=384, and the seed-to-seed spread narrows from 0.15 at N=8 to 0.005 at N=384. So the\", \"earlier failure was entirely a 10-sample artifact.\", \"\", \"**This is the number the Surya fine-tune has to beat.**\", \"\", \"Sweeps at N=384: weight decay is unhelpful (0 is best at 0.5607, rising monotonically to\", \"0.6834 at wd=1), and the pooling kernel is flat between 16 and 128 (0.5468 at kernel 16,\", \"0.5607 at the baseline's 32) but collapses at kernel 8 (0.7471 \u2014 262k features on 384\", \"samples). The baseline's default 32 is near-optimal.\", \"\", ] p = Path(\"experiments/README.md\") p.write_text(p.read_text() + \"\\n\".join(lines)) print(\"\\n\".join(lines[:8])) print(\"...\") print(f\"[README] appended {len(lines)} lines\") PY",
            "status": "failed",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_017nHu3YQFbSWn4Z3RAdqZEM",
            "kind": "execute",
            "raw_input": {
              "command": "python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\n\nR = Path(\"experiments/results\")\nbs = json.loads((R / \"baseline_study.json\").read_text())\nvis = json.loads((R / \"wave_visibility.json\").read_text())\nrep = bs[\"reproduction\"]\ncurve = bs[\"learning_curve\"]\n\nlines = [\"\", \"## Results so far (tasks 1.1 and 1.2; task 2.4 is in `results/task_2_4_answer.md`)\", \"\"]\n\nlines += [\n    \"### 1.1 \u2014 the wave is visible in the representation the baseline is given\", \"\",\n    \"`results/task_1_1_wave_visibility.png` shows three matched wave / no-wave pairs at three\",\n    \"levels of detail: AIA193 at *t*, the full-resolution running difference, and the\",\n    \"32x-mean-pooled 128x128 map that `RunningDifferenceLogisticModel` actually consumes.\",\n    \"Because the negative is the same event one hour earlier, the comparison is controlled for\",\n    \"active region, limb position and epoch of the solar cycle.\",\n    \"\",\n    \"Max |pooled| in the wave sample against its own matched control:\", \"\",\n    \"| event | wave | no wave | ratio |\",\n    \"|---|---|---|---|\",\n    \"| 2010-06-12T00:30 | 1.5719 | 0.3588 | 4.4x |\",\n    \"| 2010-08-07T17:55 | 1.1573 | 0.1422 | 8.1x |\",\n    \"| 2010-12-31T04:18 | 0.4204 | 0.1814 | 2.3x |\",\n    \"\",\n    \"So the signal survives the 32x pooling. Whatever limits the baseline, it is not that the\",\n    \"wave is invisible at 128x128.\",\n    \"\",\n    \"**Caveat worth carrying into any conclusion.** The bright running-difference structure is\",\n    \"dominated by the eruption *source region* \u2014 a compact brightening plus a dimming \u2014 not by\",\n    \"the propagating wave front. A classifier trained on this may be learning \\\"is there a\",\n    \"bright compact eruption right now\\\", which is correlated with but not the same as \\\"is there\",\n    \"an EUV wave\\\".\",\n    \"\",\n]\n\nbest = vis[\"best_offset_min\"]\nat30 = vis[\"median_pooled_snr_at_catalog_offset_30\"]\nlines += [\n    \"### 1.1 extended \u2014 is +30 min a good place to sample a positive?\", \"\",\n    \"This was the plan's largest scientific risk: positives sit at onset +30 min, so their\",\n    \"running difference spans +18 to +30 min, and if EUV wave contrast peaked early and decayed\",\n    \"by then, the *label timing* rather than the sample count would be the binding constraint.\",\n    \"\",\n    f\"Measured on {vis['n_events']} events, contrast against each event's own quiet-Sun control\",\n    \"(its negative sample's running difference at -30 min), on-disk only:\", \"\",\n    \"| requested offset | achieved | median pooled SNR |\",\n    \"|---|---|---|\",\n]\nfor off, snr in vis[\"median_pooled_snr_by_offset\"].items():\n    lines.append(f\"| +{off} min | +{vis['achieved_offsets_median'][str(off)]:.0f} min | {snr:.2f} |\")\nlines += [\n    \"\",\n    f\"**The risk did not materialize, and the effect runs the other way.** Contrast *rises* with\",\n    f\"offset: it is 1.49 at +12 min and peaks at {vis['best_median_pooled_snr']:.2f} at \"\n    f\"+{best:.0f} min. At the catalog's +30 min it is {at30:.2f} \u2014 \"\n    f\"{vis['decay_from_best_to_30_pct']:.0f}% below the peak, still 2.5x the quiet Sun.\",\n    \"So +30 min is an acceptable sampling point, the re-timed catalog the plan held in reserve\",\n    \"is unnecessary, and sample count remains the binding constraint.\",\n    \"\",\n]\n\nlines += [\n    \"### 1.2 \u2014 the 10-sample run was memorization, and more images do help\", \"\",\n    \"**The overfit reproduces.** Refitting on the 10 samples `max_samples: 10` actually selects\",\n    f\"(the earliest 5 event pairs, {rep['dates'][0]} to {rep['dates'][-1]} \u2014 `waveDSDataset`\",\n    \"head-slices a time-sorted frame, so the cap is a chronological bias, not a sample):\", \"\",\n    f\"- training loss {rep['train_loss_first']:.3f} -> {rep['train_loss_last']:.4f}, \"\n    f\"training accuracy {rep['train_accuracy_last']:.2f}\",\n    f\"- validation loss {rep['val_loss_first']:.3f} -> {rep['val_loss_last']:.3f} (rising)\",\n    f\"- validation AUROC below chance throughout, and **exactly frozen over the last two thirds\",\n    f\"  of training** (spread {rep['val_auroc_tail_spread']:.4f})\",\n    \"\",\n    \"The frozen AUROC is the diagnostic part: the *ranking* of the validation samples stops\",\n    \"changing, so the model is only rescaling a direction fixed in the first few steps. It does\",\n    \"not freeze from epoch 0 as `version_3`'s did, because validation here is the 24-sample\",\n    \"balanced split rather than `version_3`'s 27-sample set at the looser 4-day tolerance \u2014 so\",\n    \"the fingerprint differs while the diagnosis stands.\",\n    \"\",\n    \"**And validation loss does improve with more images.** Event-level stratified, nested\",\n    \"subsets, median over 5 seeds:\", \"\",\n    \"| N | best val BCE | val AUROC |\",\n    \"|---|---|---|\",\n]\nfor c in curve:\n    lines.append(f\"| {c['n_train']} | {c['best_val_loss_median']:.4f} | \"\n                 f\"{c['best_val_auroc_median']:.3f} |\")\nlines += [\n    \"\",\n    f\"`ConstantProbabilityModel`, which learns only the base rate, scores \"\n    f\"{bs['constant_probability']['val_loss']:.4f} \u2014 the same as chance (ln 2 = 0.6931) on a\",\n    \"balanced split. The running-difference baseline reaches **0.5607 BCE / 0.812 AUROC** at\",\n    \"N=384, and the seed-to-seed spread narrows from 0.15 at N=8 to 0.005 at N=384. So the\",\n    \"earlier failure was entirely a 10-sample artifact.\",\n    \"\",\n    \"**This is the number the Surya fine-tune has to beat.**\",\n    \"\",\n    \"Sweeps at N=384: weight decay is unhelpful (0 is best at 0.5607, rising monotonically to\",\n    \"0.6834 at wd=1), and the pooling kernel is flat between 16 and 128 (0.5468 at kernel 16,\",\n    \"0.5607 at the baseline's 32) but collapses at kernel 8 (0.7471 \u2014 262k features on 384\",\n    \"samples). The baseline's default 32 is near-optimal.\",\n    \"\",\n]\n\np = Path(\"experiments/README.md\")\np.write_text(p.read_text() + \"\\n\".join(lines))\nprint(\"\\n\".join(lines[:8]))\nprint(\"...\")\nprint(f\"[README] appended {len(lines)} lines\")\nPY",
              "description": "Record completed findings in the README"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
