      "id": "59ae76c8-57f5-4769-82f2-c305fc2923a1",
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "Trained: **yes**. On wandb: **no** \u2014 and that's my miss, not a wandb problem.\n\n## What actually happened\n\n`run_baseline_study.py` contains **zero** wandb calls. I grepped all four Phase 1\u20133 scripts \u2014 `run_baseline_study.py`, `plot_task_1_1.py`, `wave_visibility_scan.py`, `extract_baseline_features.py` \u2014 and not one of them mentions wandb. They write PNG + JSON to `experiments/results/` and nothing else. Your instruction was \"save plots in wandb and also in the machine\"; I did the machine half only for the entire baseline arm.\n\nSo in project `wave_classification` the only things from today are the two GPU-side runs: the smoke test at 16:14 and the killed `probe_lr3e-5` at 16:52 (setup logs, no metrics \u2014 it died before step 1). Nothing from the baseline. `4_finetune_wave_1D.py` does log to wandb properly; the CPU experiment scripts never did.\n\nThe training itself did happen \u2014 47 logistic fits: the 10-sample 1.2 reproduction, 35 learning-curve fits (7 values of N \u00d7 5 seeds), 6 weight-decay, 5 pooling-kernel. All the numbers I showed you come from those.\n\n## A second thing you should know\n\n`run_baseline_study.py` does **not** import `RunningDifferenceLogisticModel` from `models/simple_baseline.py`. It reimplements that computation on the cached features \u2014 `torch.nn.Linear(n_features, 1)` + BCEWithLogits on a 32\u00d732 mean-pooled AIA193 running difference. My plan claimed the class was \"reused as-is\"; for this one class that was wrong.\n\nThe computation is equivalent \u2014 the cache stores an 8\u00d7 mean pool (4096\u2192512) and the study re-pools by 4 (512\u2192128), and two successive uniform non-overlapping means compose exactly into a single 32\u00d7 mean pool, matching the class's `pool_kernel=32` with uniform 1/1024 weights, in signum-log space, with T ordered `[t_prev, t_now]`. But it is a reimplementation, and that's worth stating plainly rather than leaving in a docstring.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd wandb logging to `run_baseline_study.py` and re-run it. It's CPU-only on cached features so it costs a few minutes and no S3 \u2014 and re-running rather than just uploading the PNGs is what gets you real per-epoch curves in wandb for the 1.2 reproduction and the learning curve, instead of a static image attachment. Phase 1 extraction does not need redoing; the features are on disk. I'll also push the task 1.1 and visibility figures up as media, and add a check to the schedule so a run that fails to log to wandb is visible in the log.",
      "mentions": [],
      "time": 1789670105.4977891,
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false
