      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "type": "msg",
      "time": 1789671084.12544,
      "body": "The n10 reproduction is training. Status while it runs:\n\n- **wandb is live**: run `baseline_rd_n10` at `wave_classification/runs/ff6stx1v` \u2014 the missing-from-wandb defect is fixed for this arm.\n- **Nothing new was written.** The run goes through `4_finetune_wave_1D.py --train_baseline`, which instantiates `RunningDifferenceLogisticModel` from `models/simple_baseline.py` with the notebook's `pool_kernel=32` default and the same `partial(destandardize_channels, channel_order=cfg.data.channels, scalers=scalers)` preprocess hook. The **16,385 parameters** printed in the log is the notebook's exact count.\n- **Metrics are shared by construction**, not by copy: `build_metrics()` is called at line 346, *before* the `if train_baseline:` branch, so this baseline and every later Surya run use one identical set of four `WaveMetrics` modes. They cannot drift.\n- **lr had to be passed explicitly.** The plan said \"the config's lr\", but `config_wave_full.yaml` carries Surya's `1e-4`; the notebook's `0.01` lives in `config_script.yaml`. I passed `--lr 0.01` so the loss trajectory matches the notebook's.\n\nTwo trainer-level settings differ from the notebook, deliberately, because they are the shared instrument the Surya runs also use: `precision=\"bf16-mixed\"` (the notebook ran fp32) and `gradient_clip_val=1.0`. Neither touches model, loss or metrics; the 32\u00d7 average pool stays in fp32 under autocast, and BCE-with-logits is on autocast's fp32 list, so the only bf16 rounding is on the pooled features and weights.\n\nI'll report the curves when it finishes, then launch `baseline_rd_n384` (the number Surya has to beat) before any task 2 work.",
      "id": "4d484631-bd58-4cd2-9308-ebb2fc9db6b8",
