      "time": 1789674179.1269379,
      "raw_time": false,
      "mentions": []
    },
    {
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "body": "",
      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "type": "msg",
      "id": "8338416f-022f-44f7-91f5-aae95edb9b6d",
      "time": 1789674179.1922727,
      "metadata": {
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "raw_output": [
              {
                "text": "Full structural map of `/home/jovyan/surya_workshop2026/downstream_apps/test/1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb` (46 cells, kernel `conda-env-jovyan-surya_WS-py`, Python 3.12.14).\n\n## Cell-by-cell map\n\n| idx | type | exec | content |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | md | \u2013 | `# Two trainable baselines for wave classification` \u2026 |\n| 1 | md | \u2013 | `## Set your cuda visible device` \u2026 |\n| 2 | code | 1 | `import os` / `os.environ[\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\"] = \"0\"` |\n| 3 | code | 2 | Sets `CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG=\":4096:8\"`; imports `sys`, `DataLoader`, `numpy as np`, `torch`, `yaml`, `lightning as L`, `ModelCheckpoint`, `CSVLogger, WandbLogger`; `sys.path.append(\"../../\")`; `from workshop_infrastructure.utils import build_scalers`; `torch.set_float32_matmul_precision('medium')` |\n| 4 | md | \u2013 | `## Load configuration` |\n| 5 | code | 30 | `from downstream_apps.test.configs import load_wave_config` / `cfg = load_wave_config(\"./configs/config_script.yaml\")` / print job_id |\n| 6 | md | \u2013 | `## Download assets` |\n| 7 | code | 5 | `from workshop_infrastructure.assets import ensure_assets` / `ensure_assets(cfg, which=[\"scalers\"])` / `scalers = build_scalers(info=cfg.data.scalers_path)` / print channel count |\n| 8 | md | \u2013 | `## Define Downstream (DS) dataset` |\n| 9 | code | 6 | `from downstream_apps.test.datasets.wave_dataset import waveDSDataset` |\n| 10 | code | 7 | the `build_helio_dataloaders(...)` call (verbatim below) + `batch_size = cfg.batch_size` + print. Output: `train: 10 samples \\| val: 10 samples \\| batch_size: 2` |\n| 11 | md | \u2013 | \"Training and validation get separate datasets and dataloaders\u2026\" |\n| 12 | code | 8 | `print(\"kernel alive check\")` |\n| 13 | code | 9 | `batch = next(iter(train_data_loader))`; prints batch shapes; `n_channels = len(cfg.data.channels)`; `aia193_index = cfg.data.channels.index(\"aia193\")`; `img_size = batch[\"ts\"].shape[-1]`; print |\n| 14 | md | \u2013 | `## Define simple baseline models` |\n| 15 | code | 10 | `from downstream_apps.test.models.simple_baseline import (ConstantProbabilityModel, RunningDifferenceLogisticModel, destandardize_channels,)` |\n| 16 | md | \u2013 | \"We can now test that both models manipulate a batch\u2026\" |\n| 17 | code | 32 | `model_constant = ConstantProbabilityModel()` / `model_running_diff = RunningDifferenceLogisticModel(channel_index=aia193_index, img_size=img_size)` |\n| 18 | md | \u2013 | \"Now we can pass a batch to each model\u2026\" |\n| 19 | code | 12 | `batch = next(iter(train_data_loader))`; `batch_logspace = destandardize_channels(batch, channel_order=cfg.data.channels, scalers=scalers)`; `output_constant = model_constant.forward(batch)[:, 0]`; `output_running_diff = model_running_diff.forward(batch_logspace)[:, 0]`; two prints |\n| 20 | md | \u2013 | `## Define your metrics` |\n| 21 | code | 13 | `from downstream_apps.test.metrics.template_metrics import WaveMetrics` |\n| 22 | code | 14 | `def make_metrics()` (verbatim below) + `demo_metrics = make_metrics()` |\n| 23 | md | \u2013 | \"Now they can be evaluated on a model's output and our ground truth\u2026\" |\n| 24 | code | 15 | `demo_metrics[\"train_loss\"](output_running_diff, batch[\"forecast\"])` |\n| 25 | md | \u2013 | \"Then a training evaluation that will not backpropagate\u2026\" |\n| 26 | code | 16 | `demo_metrics[\"train_metrics\"](output_running_diff, batch[\"forecast\"])` |\n| 27 | md | \u2013 | \"In the validation evaluation metrics we report both accuracy and AUROC.\" |\n| 28 | code | 17 | `demo_metrics[\"val_metrics\"](output_running_diff, batch[\"forecast\"])` |\n| 29 | md | \u2013 | `## Define your PyTorch ligthning module` |\n| 30 | code | 18 | `from downstream_apps.test.lightning_modules.pl_simple_baseline import WaveLightningModule` |\n| 31 | md | \u2013 | `## Set your global seeds` |\n| 32 | code | 31 | `L.seed_everything(42, workers=True)` |\n| 33 | md | \u2013 | `## Intialize Lightning modules` |\n| 34 | code | 33 | `from functools import partial`; the two `WaveLightningModule(...)` builds (verbatim below) |\n| 35 | md | \u2013 | `## Logging` |\n| 36 | code | 25 | comment-only cell: \"WandB is now authenticated via `wandb login` (stored in ~/.netrc as lloverasdiego / surya-ws2), so WandbLogger below logs live \u2014 no offline/disabled override needed.\" No outputs. |\n| 37 | code | 21 | `project_name = cfg.wandb_project` + `def make_loggers(run_name)` (verbatim below) |\n| 38 | md | \u2013 | `## Initialize trainer` |\n| 39 | code | 34 | `max_epochs = cfg.max_epochs` + both `L.Trainer(...)` (verbatim below) |\n| 40 | md | \u2013 | `## Fit the models` |\n| 41 | code | 38 | **entirely commented out**: `#trainer_constant.fit(lit_model_constant, train_data_loader, val_data_loader)` \u2014 but still carries 22 stale outputs (HTML/progress bars) from an earlier live run |\n| 42 | code | 29 | `wandb.finish()` \u2014 **errors**: `NameError: name 'wandb' is not defined` |\n| 43 | code | 23 | `cfg.wandb_entity = \"lloverasdiego-grupo-de-estudios-en-heliofisica-de-mendoza\"` / print |\n| 44 | code | 24 | `trainer_running_diff.fit(lit_model_running_diff, train_data_loader, val_data_loader)` \u2014 ran, 21 outputs; first stderr line warns \"There is a wandb run already in progress and newly created instances of `WandbLogger` will reuse this run\u2026 call `wandb.finish()` before instantiating `WandbLogger`\" |\n| 45 | md | \u2013 | `## Conclusion` |\n\nNote the execution counts are badly out of order (30, 5, 6, 7 \u2026 21, 34, 38, 29, 23, 24), so the notebook's saved state does **not** reflect a clean top-to-bottom run. In particular cells 43 (entity override, exec 23) and 37 (`make_loggers`, exec 21) ran *before* 39 (`L.Trainer`, exec 34), and 42 (`wandb.finish`, exec 29) ran before 44 (`fit`, exec 24)\u2026 no, before 39/34 \u2014 the fit at 44 (exec 24) predates the current Trainer construction at exec 34.\n\n## Answers\n\n**1. Dataset/dataloader construction \u2014 cell 10** (dataset class imported at cell 9; `batch_size` only read at the end of cell 10 as `batch_size = cfg.batch_size`, never passed to the builder).\n\n```python\nfrom workshop_infrastructure.datasets.builders import build_helio_dataloaders\n\ntrain_data_loader, val_data_loader = build_helio_dataloaders(\n    cfg,\n    waveDSDataset,\n    scalers=scalers,\n    num_workers=0,\n    #### Downstream (DS) specific parameters\n    return_surya_stack=True,\n    max_number_of_samples=cfg.data.max_samples,\n    time_delta_input_minutes=[-12, 0],   # t_prev (one AIA cadence step earlier), t_now\n    n_input_timestamps=2,\n    ds_class_column=cfg.data.ds_class_column,\n    label_transform=lambda s: (s == \"wave\").astype(np.float32),\n    ds_wave_index_path=cfg.data.wave_index_path,\n    ds_time_column=cfg.data.ds_time_column,\n    ds_time_tolerance=cfg.data.ds_time_tolerance,\n    ds_match_direction=cfg.data.ds_match_direction,\n)\n```\nThere is **no `task_kwargs=` keyword** in the actual call \u2014 the markdown at cell 10's comment block and cell 8 talk about \"task_kwargs override the config-derived defaults\", but the wave-specific args are passed as flat kwargs. `batch_size` is not passed either (builder takes it from `cfg`). Resulting sizes: 10 train / 10 val, batch_size 2.\n\n**2. Config \u2014 cell 5**: `load_wave_config(\"./configs/config_script.yaml\")` from `downstream_apps.test.configs`. (Not `load_config`.) `cfg` is mutated afterwards at cell 43 (`cfg.wandb_entity`).\n\n**3. Scalers \u2014 cells 3 and 7**: import `build_scalers` from `workshop_infrastructure.utils` at cell 3; built at cell 7 via `scalers = build_scalers(info=cfg.data.scalers_path)`, after `ensure_assets(cfg, which=[\"scalers\"])`.\n\n**4. `models/simple_baseline.py` import \u2014 cell 15 only**, importing exactly three names: `ConstantProbabilityModel`, `RunningDifferenceLogisticModel`, `destandardize_channels`.\n\n**5. Baseline instantiation \u2014 cell 17**: `ConstantProbabilityModel()` (no args) and `RunningDifferenceLogisticModel(channel_index=aia193_index, img_size=img_size)` (both derived in cell 13). Wrapped into Lightning modules at cell 34:\n```python\nlit_model_constant = WaveLightningModule(\n    model_constant, make_metrics(), lr=cfg.learning_rate, batch_size=batch_size,\n)\npreprocess_fn = partial(destandardize_channels, channel_order=cfg.data.channels, scalers=scalers)\nlit_model_running_diff = WaveLightningModule(\n    model_running_diff, make_metrics(), lr=cfg.learning_rate, batch_size=batch_size,\n    preprocess_fn=preprocess_fn,\n)\n```\n\n**6. `make_metrics()` \u2014 cell 22; `make_loggers()` \u2014 cell 37.**\n```python\ndef make_metrics() -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Build a fresh dict of WaveMetrics instances. ...\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'train_loss': WaveMetrics(\"train_loss\"),\n        'val_loss': WaveMetrics(\"val_loss\"),\n        'train_metrics': WaveMetrics(\"train_metrics\"),\n        'val_metrics': WaveMetrics(\"val_metrics\"),\n    }\n\ndemo_metrics = make_metrics()\n```\n```python\nproject_name = cfg.wandb_project\ndef make_loggers(run_name: str) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Build a fresh WandB + CSV logger pair for one baseline's run.\"\"\"\n    wandb_logger = WandbLogger(\n        entity=cfg.wandb_entity,\n        project=project_name,\n        name=run_name,\n        log_model=False,\n        save_dir=\"./wandb/wandb_tmp\",\n    )\n    csv_logger = CSVLogger(\"runs\", name=f\"{project_name}_{run_name}\")\n    return [wandb_logger, csv_logger]\n```\nYes \u2014 `make_loggers` creates a `WandbLogger` with `entity=cfg.wandb_entity`, `project=cfg.wandb_project` (via `project_name`, captured as a module-level global at definition time), `name=run_name`, `log_model=False`, `save_dir=\"./wandb/wandb_tmp\"`, plus a `CSVLogger(\"runs\", name=f\"{project_name}_{run_name}\")`.\n\n**7. Trainers \u2014 cell 39; fits \u2014 cells 41 (commented out) and 44 (live).**\n```python\nmax_epochs = cfg.max_epochs\n\ntrainer_constant = L.Trainer(\n    max_epochs=max_epochs,\n    accelerator=\"auto\",\n    devices=\"auto\",\n    logger=make_loggers(\"baseline_constant_prob\"),\n    callbacks=[ModelCheckpoint(monitor=\"val_loss\", mode=\"min\", save_top_k=1)],\n    log_every_n_steps=2,\n)\n\ntrainer_running_diff = L.Trainer(\n    max_epochs=max_epochs,\n    accelerator=\"auto\",\n    devices=\"auto\",\n    logger=make_loggers(\"baseline_running_diff\"),\n    callbacks=[ModelCheckpoint(monitor=\"val_loss\", mode=\"min\", save_top_k=1)],\n    log_every_n_steps=2,\n)\n```\nBecause both `make_loggers(...)` calls happen in this one cell, two `WandbLogger`s are constructed back to back with no `wandb.finish()` between them \u2014 that is the source of the \"wandb run already in progress\u2026 will reuse this run\" warning in cell 44's output. Both baselines therefore log into the same wandb run.\n\n**8. wandb API calls**: only one \u2014 cell 42, exact line `wandb.finish()`, which raised `NameError: name 'wandb' is not defined` because `wandb` is never imported (cell 3 imports only `WandbLogger` from `lightning.pytorch.loggers`). There is **no** `wandb.init` and no `wandb.log` anywhere.\n\n**9. Plotting**: none. No `matplotlib`, `plt.`, `seaborn`, `savefig`, or figure-logging anywhere in the notebook. All visual output is Lightning's progress bars / model-summary tables.\n\n**10. Test split**: no. Only `train_data_loader` and `val_data_loader` exist; there is no test dataset, no test dataloader, no `trainer.test(...)` or `trainer.predict(...)`. Every occurrence of the string \"test\" is either the package path `downstream_apps.test.*` or prose (\"test that both models manipulate a batch\"). The conclusion markdown (cell 45) points at `val_metric_accuracy` / `val_metric_auroc` in WandB or `runs/` as the evaluation surface.\n\nUseful side notes for whatever you are about to modify: `img_size` and `aia193_index` (cell 13) are consumed by cell 17, so cell 13 must run before model construction; `batch_size` (cell 10) is consumed by cell 34; `project_name` (cell 37) is a global closed over by `make_loggers`, so changing `cfg.wandb_project` after cell 37 has no effect until cell 37 is re-run, whereas `cfg.wandb_entity` is read at call time inside `make_loggers` and so *is* picked up by cell 43's late override.",
