              "prompt": "Repo root is /home/jovyan/surya_workshop2026. All paths below are under /home/jovyan/surya_workshop2026/downstream_apps/test/.\n\nRead these files IN FULL and report their complete public API (every function/class, its exact signature, its docstring summary, and what it returns):\n\n1. models/simple_baseline.py  \u2014 this file was recently modified (git status shows it as M). I need to know its CURRENT contents exactly: every class and function, full signatures, default argument values, and the full body of forward() for each model class. Pay special attention to any NEW functionality (anything beyond a ConstantProbabilityModel, a RunningDifferenceLogisticModel and a destandardize_channels function). Also run `cd /home/jovyan/surya_workshop2026 && git diff -- downstream_apps/test/models/simple_baseline.py` and report the diff so I can see what changed versus the committed version.\n\n2. experiments/wave_common.py \u2014 report every function with its exact signature and a one-line description of what it does. I especially need: anything that builds wave datasets or dataloaders, anything that takes an event-level stratified subset of the training set, anything that reports dataset statistics (sample counts, class balance, pair counts), and any assertion helpers. Quote the full body of the dataset-building and subsetting functions.\n\n3. datasets/wave_dataset.py and datasets/wave_dataset_memory.py \u2014 what class(es) do they define, what are the constructor signatures, how do they differ from each other, and which one reads through RAM versus writing to a disk cache?\n\n4. metrics/template_metrics.py \u2014 the WaveMetrics class: its constructor signature, the exact set of valid mode strings, and what each mode returns from its __call__/forward.\n\n5. lightning_modules/pl_simple_baseline.py \u2014 the WaveLightningModule constructor signature (every argument with defaults) and the exact list of metric names it passes to self.log() in training_step and validation_step.\n\nReport as a structured reference document. Include exact code for signatures and for the dataset-building/subsetting functions. Read-only \u2014 do not modify anything.",
