                "text": "## Part A \u2014 `2_finetune_template_1D_diego.ipynb` structural map\n\n48 cells (0\u201347). Kernel state: exec counts 1\u201322 run in order; the last two code cells (44 `trainer.fit`, 46 `wandb.finish`) have `execution_count: None` (never run).\n\n| idx | type | exec | content |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | md | \u2013 | `# PyTorch Lightning fine-tuning template` |\n| 1 | md | \u2013 | `## Set your cuda visible device` |\n| 2 | code | 1 | `import os` / `os.environ[\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\"] = \"0\"` |\n| 3 | code | 2 | sets `CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG=\":4096:8\"` before torch; imports `sys`, `DataLoader`, `torch`, `yaml`, `lightning as L`, `ModelCheckpoint`, `CSVLogger, WandbLogger`; `sys.path.append(\"../../\")`; `from workshop_infrastructure.utils import build_scalers` and `apply_peft_lora`; `torch.set_float32_matmul_precision('medium')`. **No `import numpy as np` here.** |\n| 4 | md | \u2013 | `## Load configuration` |\n| 5 | code | 3 | `from downstream_apps.test.configs import load_wave_config` / `cfg = load_wave_config(\"./configs/config_script.yaml\")` / print job_id |\n| 6 | md | \u2013 | `## Download assets` |\n| 7 | code | 4 | `from workshop_infrastructure.assets import ensure_assets` / `ensure_assets(cfg, which=[\"scalers\", \"weights\"])` / `scalers = build_scalers(info=cfg.data.scalers_path)` |\n| 8 | md | \u2013 | `### Typed configuration, and how to extend it\u2026` |\n| 9 | md | \u2013 | `## Define Downstream (DS) datasets` |\n| 10 | code | 5 | `from downstream_apps.test.datasets.wave_dataset import waveDSDataset` |\n| 11 | code | 6 | **the dataloader build \u2014 quoted in full below** |\n| 12 | md | \u2013 | note that train/val differ only in index + `phase` |\n| 13 | code | 7 | `batch = next(iter(train_data_loader))` + shape print |\n| 14 | md | \u2013 | `## Initialize the HelioSpectformer model` |\n| 15 | code | 8 | `from workshop_infrastructure.models.finetune_models import HelioSpectformer1D` |\n| 16 | md | \u2013 | \"Now the config file really comes into bear\u2026\" |\n| 17 | code | 9 | `model = HelioSpectformer1D.from_config(cfg.model, num_outputs=1, dtype=cfg.dtype, use_latitude_in_learned_flow=cfg.use_latitude_in_learned_flow)` |\n| 18 | md | \u2013 | `## Load model weights` |\n| 19 | code | 10 | `from workshop_infrastructure.utils import load_pretrained_weights` / `load_pretrained_weights(model, cfg.model.pretrained_path)` |\n| 20 | md | \u2013 | `## To LoRA or not to Lora` |\n| 21 | code | 11 | freeze `backbone.*` if `cfg.model.freeze_backbone`; `model = apply_peft_lora(model, cfg.model.lora_config)` if `cfg.model.use_lora`; trainable-param count print |\n| 22 | md | \u2013 | \"We can now test that this model manipulates a batch\u2026\" |\n| 23 | code | 12 | `batch = next(iter(train_data_loader))` / `output = model.forward(batch)` / `output` |\n| 24 | md | \u2013 | `## Define your metrics` |\n| 25 | code | 13 | `from downstream_apps.test.metrics.template_metrics import WaveMetrics` |\n| 26 | code | 14 | four module-level singletons \u2014 quoted below |\n| 27 | md | \u2013 | \"\u2026binary cross-entropy with logits\" |\n| 28 | code | 15 | `train_loss_metrics(output, batch[\"forecast\"])` |\n| 29 | md | \u2013 | training-eval-metrics note |\n| 30 | code | 16 | `train_evaluation_metrics(output, batch[\"forecast\"])` |\n| 31 | md | \u2013 | \"\u2026accuracy and **AUROC**\" |\n| 32 | code | 17 | `validation_evaluation_metrics(output, batch[\"forecast\"])` |\n| 33 | md | \u2013 | `## Define your PyTorch ligthning module` |\n| 34 | code | 18 | `from downstream_apps.test.lightning_modules.pl_simple_baseline import WaveLightningModule` |\n| 35 | md | \u2013 | `## Set your global seeds` |\n| 36 | code | 19 | `L.seed_everything(42, workers=True)` |\n| 37 | md | \u2013 | `## Intialize Lightning module` |\n| 38 | code | 20 | metrics dict + `lit_model = WaveLightningModule(model, metrics, lr=cfg.learning_rate, batch_size=batch_size)` |\n| 39 | md | \u2013 | `## Logging` |\n| 40 | code | 21 | `WandbLogger(...)` + `CSVLogger(\"runs\", name=project_name)` \u2014 quoted below |\n| 41 | md | \u2013 | `## Initialize trainer` |\n| 42 | code | 22 | `L.Trainer(...)` \u2014 quoted below |\n| 43 | md | \u2013 | `## Fit the model` |\n| 44 | code | **None** | `trainer.fit(lit_model, train_data_loader, val_data_loader)` |\n| 45 | md | \u2013 | `## Close the WandB run` |\n| 46 | code | **None** | `import wandb` / `if wandb.run is not None: wandb.finish()` \u2026 |\n| 47 | md | \u2013 | `## Conclusion` |\n\n### A.1 \u2014 dataset/dataloader construction (cell **11**)\n\n```python\nfrom workshop_infrastructure.datasets.builders import build_helio_dataloaders\nimport numpy as np\ntrain_data_loader, val_data_loader = build_helio_dataloaders(\n    cfg,\n    waveDSDataset,\n    scalers=scalers,\n    num_workers=4,          # fewer workers than the script: notebooks start faster\n    #### Downstream (DS) specific parameters\n    return_surya_stack=True,\n    max_number_of_samples=cfg.data.max_samples,\n    ds_wave_index_path=cfg.data.wave_index_path,\n    ds_time_column=cfg.data.ds_time_column,\n    ds_class_column=cfg.data.ds_class_column,\n    ds_time_tolerance=cfg.data.ds_time_tolerance,\n    ds_match_direction=cfg.data.ds_match_direction,\n    label_transform=lambda s: (s == \"wave\").astype(np.float32),\n)\n\nbatch_size = cfg.batch_size\n```\n\nNote what is **absent**: no `time_delta_input_minutes`, no `n_input_timestamps`, no `seed`, no `batch_size` (all inherited from `cfg` inside the builder). Also `import numpy as np` is done *inside* this cell, not in the header cell.\n\nThe cell's own docstring-comment already flags the two gaps: \"One thing it does NOT expose is prefetch_factor, and it sets `drop_last=True` for the validation loader too \u2026 see `experiments/wave_common.py:build_wave_loader()`\".\n\n### A.2 \u2014 config\n`/home/jovyan/surya_workshop2026/downstream_apps/test/configs/config_script.yaml`, loaded with `load_wave_config` from `downstream_apps.test.configs` (cell 5). That symbol is `partial(load_config, data_cls=WaveDataConfig)` at `/home/jovyan/surya_workshop2026/downstream_apps/test/configs.py:56`.\n\n### A.3 \u2014 test dataloader\n**No.** Only `train_data_loader` and `val_data_loader`. There is no `test_data_path` usage, no third loader, and no `trainer.test(...)` / `trainer.validate(...)` call anywhere in the notebook.\n\n### A.4 \u2014 Trainer / loggers (cells 40, 42, 46)\n\n```python\nwandb_logger = WandbLogger(\n    entity=cfg.wandb_entity,\n    project=project_name,          # cfg.wandb_project\n    name=run_name,                 # \"finetune_experiment_1\"\n    log_model=False,\n    save_dir=\"./wandb/wandb_tmp\",\n)\ncsv_logger = CSVLogger(\"runs\", name=project_name)\n```\n\n```python\ntrainer = L.Trainer(\n    max_epochs=max_epochs,         # cfg.max_epochs\n    accelerator=\"auto\",\n    devices=\"auto\",\n    precision=\"bf16-mixed\",\n    gradient_clip_val=1.0,\n    logger=[wandb_logger, csv_logger],\n    callbacks=[ModelCheckpoint(monitor=\"val_loss\", mode=\"min\", save_top_k=1)],\n    log_every_n_steps=2,\n)\n```\n\nYes to `WandbLogger`; yes to a guarded `wandb.finish()` in cell 46 (`if wandb.run is not None`), but that cell was **never executed** (`execution_count: None`) \u2014 same for `trainer.fit`.\n\n### A.5 \u2014 WaveMetrics / WaveLightningModule\nYes, both. `WaveMetrics` from `downstream_apps.test.metrics.template_metrics`; four **module-level singletons** (cell 26):\n\n```python\ntrain_loss_metrics = WaveMetrics(\"train_loss\")\nval_loss_metrics = WaveMetrics(\"val_loss\")\ntrain_evaluation_metrics = WaveMetrics(\"train_metrics\")\nvalidation_evaluation_metrics = WaveMetrics(\"val_metrics\")\n```\n\nthen (cell 38) a plain dict keyed `train_loss/val_loss/train_metrics/val_metrics` and\n\n```python\nlit_model = WaveLightningModule(model, metrics, lr=cfg.learning_rate, batch_size=batch_size)\n```\n\nNo `preprocess_fn` \u2014 the Surya backbone consumes normalized `ts` directly.\n\n---\n\n## Part B \u2014 `/home/jovyan/surya_workshop2026/workshop_infrastructure/datasets/builders.py` (166 lines)\n\n### B.1 \u2014 signatures\n\n```python\ndef build_helio_datasets(\n    cfg,\n    dataset_cls: Type[Dataset],\n    scalers: Any = None,\n    **task_kwargs,\n) -> Tuple[Dataset, Dataset]:\n```\n\n```python\ndef build_helio_dataloaders(\n    cfg,\n    dataset_cls: Type[Dataset],\n    scalers: Any = None,\n    num_workers: int | None = None,\n    seed: int | None = None,\n    **task_kwargs,\n) -> Tuple[DataLoader, DataLoader]:\n```\n\nThere is no `batch_size`, `prefetch_factor`, `drop_last`, `pin_memory`, `shuffle`, or `persistent_workers` parameter. `batch_size` comes only from `cfg.batch_size`.\n\nAlso present: `_seed_worker(worker_id, base_seed)` (lines 34\u201349) and `_base_dataset_kwargs(cfg, scalers)` (lines 52\u201376), which maps `cfg` \u2192 15 dataset args including `time_delta_input_minutes=cfg.data.time_delta_input_minutes`, `n_input_timestamps=cfg.model.time_embedding.time_dim`, `rollout_steps`, `channels`, `scalers`, `drop_hmi_probability`, `use_latitude_in_learned_flow`, and the six `sdo_data_root_path`/`s3_*` fields.\n\n### B.2 \u2014 splits returned\n**train + val only.** Both functions return a 2-tuple. There is no test split anywhere in the file; only `cfg.data.train_data_path` and `cfg.data.valid_data_path` are read (lines 105\u2013106).\n\n### B.3 \u2014 `task_kwargs` threading\n\n```python\ncommon = {**_base_dataset_kwargs(cfg, scalers), **task_kwargs}\n\ntrain_dataset = dataset_cls(index_path=cfg.data.train_data_path, phase=\"train\", **common)\nval_dataset   = dataset_cls(index_path=cfg.data.valid_data_path, phase=\"val\",   **common)\n```\n\nBecause `task_kwargs` is splatted **second**, a caller-supplied key **silently overrides** the config-derived value of the same name. That is exactly the mechanism notebook 1 uses for `time_delta_input_minutes` / `n_input_timestamps`. `index_path` and `phase` are the only per-split differences; `build_helio_dataloaders` forwards `**task_kwargs` verbatim into `build_helio_datasets`.\n\n### B.4 \u2014 `drop_last` on val, `prefetch_factor`\n\n`drop_last=True` is applied to **both** loaders (it lives in the shared `loader_kwargs`), and `prefetch_factor` is **not exposed at all**. Lines 143\u2013166:\n\n```python\n    loader_kwargs = dict(\n        batch_size=cfg.batch_size,\n        num_workers=workers,\n        pin_memory=True,\n        drop_last=True,\n    )\n    if workers > 0:\n        loader_kwargs[\"multiprocessing_context\"] = \"spawn\"\n        loader_kwargs[\"persistent_workers\"] = True\n        loader_kwargs[\"worker_init_fn\"] = partial(_seed_worker, base_seed=base_seed)\n\n    shuffle_generator = torch.Generator()\n    shuffle_generator.manual_seed(base_seed)\n\n    train_loader = DataLoader(\n        train_dataset, shuffle=True, generator=shuffle_generator, **loader_kwargs\n    )\n    # No generator for validation: it is not shuffled, so there is nothing to seed.\n    val_loader = DataLoader(val_dataset, shuffle=False, **loader_kwargs)\n    return train_loader, val_loader\n```\n\nThe escape hatch already exists at `/home/jovyan/surya_workshop2026/downstream_apps/test/experiments/wave_common.py:588` \u2014 `build_wave_loader(dataset, batch_size, num_workers, prefetch_factor, seed, shuffle, drop_last)`, which imports the private `_seed_worker` deliberately and adds `prefetch_factor` only when `num_workers > 0`, and attaches the generator only when `shuffle`.\n\n### B.5 \u2014 `num_workers`, `generator`, `worker_init_fn`\n\n```python\nworkers   = cfg.num_workers if num_workers is None else num_workers   # cfg default: 8\nbase_seed = cfg.seed        if seed        is None else seed           # cfg default: 42\n```\n\n- `num_workers`: caller override wins, else `cfg.num_workers`. Crossing 0 changes three other kwargs at once (`multiprocessing_context=\"spawn\"`, `persistent_workers=True`, `worker_init_fn`), because those three are rejected outright at `num_workers == 0`.\n- `generator`: a fresh `torch.Generator` seeded with `base_seed`, passed **only** to the train loader.\n- `worker_init_fn`: `partial(_seed_worker, base_seed=base_seed)`, which seeds Python `random`, NumPy and torch per worker as `(base_seed + worker_id) % 2**32`. Supplying it deliberately displaces Lightning's auto-injected `pl_worker_init_function`.\n\n---\n\n## Part C \u2014 notebook 1 vs notebook 2: dataset/dataloader diff\n\nNotebook 1's call is at `/home/jovyan/surya_workshop2026/downstream_apps/test/1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb` **cell 10**; notebook 2's at `2_finetune_template_1D_diego.ipynb` **cell 11**. Both call `build_helio_dataloaders(cfg, waveDSDataset, scalers=scalers, ...)` with the same config file. Exhaustive diff:\n\n| argument | nb1 (cell 10) | nb2 (cell 11) | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `num_workers` | `0` | `4` | **Real difference.** Only nb2 gets `multiprocessing_context=\"spawn\"`, `persistent_workers=True`, `worker_init_fn=_seed_worker`. nb1 loads in-process with **no** `_seed_worker` at all, so its augmentation RNG (`RandomChannelMaskerTransform` \u2192 Python `random`) draws from the ambient main-process state instead of the seeded per-worker state. |\n| `time_delta_input_minutes` | `[-12, 0]` (explicit override) | not passed \u2192 `cfg.data.time_delta_input_minutes` | **Currently a no-op.** `config_script.yaml:48` is already `[-12, 0]`. Values identical. |\n| `n_input_timestamps` | `2` (explicit override) | not passed \u2192 `cfg.model.time_embedding.time_dim` | **Currently a no-op.** `config_script.yaml:154` is already `time_dim: 2`. Values identical. |\n| `return_surya_stack` | `True` | `True` | same |\n| `max_number_of_samples` | `cfg.data.max_samples` | `cfg.data.max_samples` | same (`10`) |\n| `ds_wave_index_path` | `cfg.data.wave_index_path` | same | same |\n| `ds_time_column` | `cfg.data.ds_time_column` | same | same |\n| `ds_class_column` | `cfg.data.ds_class_column` | same | same |\n| `ds_time_tolerance` | `cfg.data.ds_time_tolerance` | same | same |\n| `ds_match_direction` | `cfg.data.ds_match_direction` | same | same |\n| `label_transform` | `lambda s: (s == \"wave\").astype(np.float32)` | identical lambda | same behavior; two separate inline lambdas |\n| `scalers` | `scalers` | `scalers` | same |\n| `seed` | not passed \u2192 `cfg.seed` | not passed \u2192 `cfg.seed` | same (42) |\n| `batch_size` | from `cfg.batch_size` inside builder | same | same (2) |\n| kwarg ordering | `ds_class_column`/`label_transform` before the `ds_*` block | grouped `ds_*` then `label_transform` | cosmetic |\n| `np` import site | header cell 3 (`import numpy as np`) | inside cell 11 | cosmetic |\n\n**Bottom line for the unification goal:** the *datasets* are already byte-for-byte equivalent \u2014 the only substantive divergence is `num_workers` (0 vs 4), which changes the loader, not the data. The two explicit overrides in nb1 (`time_delta_input_minutes=[-12, 0]`, `n_input_timestamps=2`) are now redundant duplicates of the YAML, and their surrounding comment is **stale**: it claims \"`cfg.model.time_embedding.time_dim` stays 1 in the YAML, unaffected,\" but the YAML was since changed to `time_dim: 2` (with the old `time_dim: 1` left commented at line 152 explaining that it silently left the tokenizer random). Deleting those two overrides makes nb1's call textually identical to nb2's apart from `num_workers`, and removes the trap where changing the YAML would no longer change nb1.\n\nThree additional non-dataset differences worth knowing if you factor the two calls into one shared helper:\n\n- nb1 calls `ensure_assets(cfg, which=[\"scalers\"])`; nb2 needs `[\"scalers\", \"weights\"]` (the 1.8 GB backbone). A shared dataset helper must not own that call.\n- nb1's `num_workers=0` is load-bearing per its own comment: spawned workers need to re-import a `__main__` script that doesn't exist under a Jupyter kernel. If that is true it applies to nb2 equally \u2014 nb2's `num_workers=4` is the riskier of the two, so the shared value should be `0` for notebooks (or the helper should take `num_workers` as its one parameter).\n- Neither notebook builds a test loader, and `build_helio_dataloaders` cannot produce one; a test split would need `build_helio_datasets` plus `wave_common.build_wave_loader(..., shuffle=False, drop_last=False)`.",
                "type": "text"
              }
