            "raw_output": "=== callers passing img_size (now BROKEN) ===\n1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb:324:    \"2. `RunningDifferenceLogisticModel` \u2014 AIA193(now) - AIA193(one cadence step earlier),\\n\",\n1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb:341:    \"    RunningDifferenceLogisticModel,\\n\",\n1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb:354:    \"`ConstantProbabilityModel` needs no configuration \u2014 it ignores the image. `RunningDifferenceLogisticModel`\\n\",\n1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb:376:    \"model_running_diff = RunningDifferenceLogisticModel(channel_index=aia193_index, img_size=img_size)\\n\"\n1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb:406:    \"# RunningDifferenceLogisticModel works in signum-log space, not normalized space.\\n\",\n1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb:1162:      \"0 | model | RunningDifferenceLogisticModel | 16.4 K | train | 0    \\n\",\nmodels/simple_baseline.py:135:class RunningDifferenceLogisticModel(nn.Module):\nexperiments/wave_common.py:22:3. **The running-difference feature.** ``RunningDifferenceLogisticModel`` computes it on\nexperiments/wave_common.py:462:    ``RunningDifferenceLogisticModel.forward()`` computes it per training step;\nexperiments/run_baseline_study.py:10:The model is exactly ``RunningDifferenceLogisticModel``: a 32x32 mean pool of\nexperiments/run_baseline_study.py:46:BASE_POOL = 32          # the kernel RunningDifferenceLogisticModel uses\n4_finetune_wave_1D.py:352:            RunningDifferenceLogisticModel,\n4_finetune_wave_1D.py:355:        #model = RunningDifferenceLogisticModel(\nexperiments/plot_task_1_1.py:10:   ``RunningDifferenceLogisticModel`` actually consumes. Everything the baseline can\n\n=== config_script.yaml key values ===\n15:#     s3_cache_dir \u2014 see its comment below.\n40:  channels: [aia94, aia131, aia171, aia193, aia211, aia304, aia335, aia1600,\n42:  # time_delta_input_minutes: [0]  # previous value. Combined with time_dim: 1 below it\n54:  # ds_time_tolerance: 4d         # previous value. 98.3% of train matches already land\n58:  ds_time_tolerance: 15min        # Max allowed gap between catalog and Surya timestamps\n70:  #   download    \u2014 fetch the whole file into s3_cache_dir, then open locally.\n72:  #   simplecache \u2014 fsspec read-through cache into s3_cache_dir. ~29 s on a cold fetch.\n87:  #   2. s3_cache_dir: /scratch/me/helio_cache       (here, in your own fork)\n103:  s3_cache_dir: /home/jovyan/wave_cache\n122:  max_samples: 10                 # Cap dataset size for quick experiments (null = all samples)\n135:  in_channels: 13\n152:    # time_dim: 1       # previous value -- see time_delta_input_minutes above: it is half of\n154:    time_dim: 2         # Number of input timesteps (must match time_delta_input_minutes length)\n185:  # learning_rate: 0.0001  # previous value: with only 20 gradient steps (4 epochs x 5\n186:  #   batches on max_samples=10), this was too small to move the running-diff baseline's\n187:  #   loss off chance level (~0.693) within the notebook's hardcoded max_epochs=4.\n188:  learning_rate: 0.01      # diagnostic: at this LR the same baseline drove loss from\n190:  batch_size: 2         # Per-device batch size under DDP\n191:  max_epochs: 20        # Can be overridden with --max-epochs at the CLI\n192:  num_workers: 8        # DataLoader worker processes per device (use 0 to debug in-process)\n202:  #            throughput. Measured on this template (1 epoch, max_samples: 10, one A100,\n220:  # significance. With max_samples: 10 and one epoch the number is still noise \u2014 it is\n246:  wandb_project: wave_classification\n247:  wandb_entity: lloverasdiego-grupo-de-estudios-en-heliofisica-de-mendoza      # avoid the surya-ws2 team's per-member run cap",
