      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "Audit complete. Here's what's actually wrong with `1_baseline_template_diego.ipynb`, confirmed against the current source:\n\n**Two hard errors \u2014 the notebook cannot run top to bottom:**\n- `b0b6ce02` \u2014 `RunningDifferenceLogisticModel(..., img_size=img_size)`. Your rewrite made the signature `(channel_index, pool_kernel=32)` (`models/simple_baseline.py:169`), so this is now a `TypeError`.\n- `a75db65c` \u2014 `wandb.finish()` raises `NameError`; cell 3 imports only Lightning's `WandbLogger`, never `wandb` itself.\n\n**Four silent errors \u2014 it runs but does the wrong thing:**\n- `b008c604` builds *both* Trainers in one cell, so the second `WandbLogger` reuses the first's run \u2014 both baselines land on one set of wandb axes. That's the \"wandb run already in progress\" warning in your saved output.\n- `f8a6e448` has the constant-probability fit commented out, so the base-rate reference is never trained \u2014 there's nothing to compare against.\n- `ceb1ef4f` sets `cfg.wandb_entity` *after* the loggers were already built, so it has no effect on the run that exists.\n- `70e9c5b2` \u2014 `max_samples=10` head-slices by `ds_index`, giving the 5 earliest pairs (June\u2013July 2010), plus `drop_last=True` on val, no `prefetch_factor`, and an unpicklable `lambda` that breaks any `num_workers > 0`.\n\n**Plus:** `cfg.learning_rate = 0.01` is ~2 orders too small for a 2-parameter model on a feature of order 0.1 (your own docstring says so), and there are no loss plots anywhere.\n\nFixing all of it now, starting with imports."
    },
    {
