            "title": "Read experiments/wave_common.py (589 - 648)",
            "raw_output": "589\tdef build_wave_loader(\n590\t    dataset,\n591\t    batch_size: int,\n592\t    num_workers: int,\n593\t    prefetch_factor: int | None,\n594\t    seed: int,\n595\t    shuffle: bool,\n596\t    drop_last: bool,\n597\t):\n598\t    \"\"\"Build a DataLoader with the two knobs ``build_helio_dataloaders()`` does not expose.\n599\t\n600\t    ``build_helio_dataloaders()`` is the right entry point for a normal run, but it hard-codes\n601\t    ``drop_last=True`` for *both* loaders and does not expose ``prefetch_factor``. Both matter\n602\t    here:\n603\t\n604\t    * ``drop_last=True`` on a 24-sample validation set at batch 2 is survivable, but on any\n605\t      odd-sized split it silently discards a sample \u2014 1 of 27 is 3.7% of the metric that\n606\t      selects checkpoints.\n607\t    * ``prefetch_factor`` is the only bound on worker memory. ``ts`` is\n608\t      ``(B, 13, 2, 4096, 4096)`` fp32 = 1.74 GB per sample, so worst-case resident set is\n609\t      ``num_workers * prefetch_factor * batch_size * 1.74 GB``: 27.8 GB at\n610\t      ``8 x 1 x 2``, but 55.7 GB at PyTorch's default factor of 2.\n611\t\n612\t    Everything else \u2014 spawn (the dataset holds a boto3 handle that does not survive fork),\n613\t    persistent workers, the explicit generator and the per-worker seeding \u2014 matches\n614\t    ``build_helio_dataloaders()`` exactly, by reusing its ``_seed_worker``. That function is\n615\t    private but importing it is deliberate: its whole purpose is to displace Lightning's\n616\t    auto-injected worker init, which derives worker seeds from ambient global RNG state, and\n617\t    a second copy of it here could drift out of step with the datasets it seeds.\n618\t    \"\"\"\n619\t    from functools import partial\n620\t\n621\t    from torch.utils.data import DataLoader\n622\t    from workshop_infrastructure.datasets.builders import _seed_worker\n623\t\n624\t    kwargs = dict(\n625\t        batch_size=batch_size,\n626\t        num_workers=num_workers,\n627\t        pin_memory=True,\n628\t        drop_last=drop_last,\n629\t    )\n630\t    if num_workers > 0:\n631\t        kwargs[\"multiprocessing_context\"] = \"spawn\"\n632\t        kwargs[\"persistent_workers\"] = True\n633\t        kwargs[\"worker_init_fn\"] = partial(_seed_worker, base_seed=seed)\n634\t        if prefetch_factor is not None:\n635\t            kwargs[\"prefetch_factor\"] = prefetch_factor\n636\t\n637\t    if shuffle:\n638\t        generator = torch.Generator()\n639\t        generator.manual_seed(seed)\n640\t        kwargs[\"generator\"] = generator\n641\t\n642\t    return DataLoader(dataset, shuffle=shuffle, **kwargs)\n643\t\n644\t\n645\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n646\t# Figures\n647\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n648\t",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01FnnwHDmXxc5F54CPs2g6xg",
            "kind": "read"
          }
        ]
